//@version=6
// mVWAP-BB — the operator's VWAP setups. Script version: v50 (2026-11-28). Since v30 the number
// follows TradingView's own version counter for the operator's saved script (their save 30 = v30).
// Docs: docs/vwap-setup.md — the walkthrough, changelog, and the steps for shipping
// a new version (bump the version above, recreate the alerts).
// Five setups in one script (PULLBACK, the VWAP + BB cross, the EMA cross, TURN, POP with its BACK),
// so the same two watchlist alerts carry them all (the VWAP + BB cross and the EMA cross only send
// from the 30s alert, TURN and POP / BACK from the 1m one). Each has its own "… setup on" switch: off
// = no markers and no alerts from it, and a VWAP line no setup uses isn't drawn.
// v27 removed the RECLAIM setup (FORMING / READY / GO, v1–v26) and the BB breakout
// (TOUCH / BREAKOUT / TRIGGERED, v17–v26): the operator tested all four and kept these
// two (10-28 ET). Both are in git history (v26, e38c06b) and docs/vwap-setup.md.
// v39 removed two experiments (operator, 11-15): the DIP's LIFT (v38) and the VB lanes (v29).
// They are in git history (v38, 7c7b4b9) and docs/vwap-setup.md. The EMA cross over VWAP stays
// ("I want to improve it later").
// v44 removed three more (operator, 11-22): the RSI cross with its DIP (v32–v34), the MACD cross after a DIP (v39)
// and the BASIS cross (v42). All are in git history (v43, 97546dd) and docs/vwap-setup.md §17 / §18.6.
// v45 draws one more line for the PULLBACK (section 6, at the end): the basis of a Bollinger Band
// of its own timeframe (15S by default). A line only, with no alert.
// v46 draws the same kind of line for the EMA cross setup's band cross (section 7), with its own
// switch, timeframe and length in the "EMA cross over VWAP" group.
// v47 adds a fourth setup, TURN (section 8, at the end): after a basis fell and turned up, price
// closes above it, comes back to it and bounces. Its own basis and MACD settings; sent from the
// alert on the basis's timeframe (1m).
// v48 adds a fifth setup in two steps (section 9, at the end): POP, a heads-up when a run's high
// gets well above its basis, and BACK, the entry, when the price then comes back to the basis and
// bounces. Its own basis and MACD settings; sent from the alert on the basis's timeframe (1m).
// v49 gives the POP a volume test (section 9): a POP is weak (gray, `| weak`, not announced) when
// the biggest of its candle and the two before it traded under 10 times the average of the 20
// candles before them, and so is its BACK; every POP and BACK carries the reading (`| vol 34.5x`).
// v50 puts the stock's RVol in the POP's and the BACK's message (`| rvol1 14250 | rvol5 9800`, in
// percent, section 9): a reading only, with no input and no rule of its own (two hidden plots).
// 1) PULLBACK (v10): a fast run stretches price well above a VWAP line — the
// session, month or (v14) year VWAP — and it comes back down to it.
//   PULLBACK  a close back within 5% above the line after a bar high ≥15% above it → be ready
//             (v24 trial, month and year lines: the bar's low within 5% is enough, its close
//             holding at or above the line)
//   BROKEN    a close under the line → the setup is over (the operator's exit)
//   HELD      price runs +10% from the PULLBACK close first
// Each line runs its own setup, and every message carries its touch number (the
// operator rates the first pullback after the first big move highest; our own
// data found the second as good — docs/vwap-setup.md §13.5).
// 2) VWAP + BB CROSS (v21): one candle of a timeframe you pick (5m, 1h, …) crosses
// over both a VWAP line — session, and (v22) month or year — and the upper Bollinger
// Band of another timeframe you pick (45s, 2m, 30m, …). Each line runs its own setup.
//   CROSS      the candle opened under both lines (or sitting on the lower one) and a
//              30s close inside it is above both → the alert, while the candle is open
//   RETEST     (v28) after the VB candle closes, price comes back to the line it crossed
//              (within 1%) and (v30) the candle closes above it → the alert, at that close, with a
//              stop under the pullback's low (the operator's entry; v25–v27 had LEVEL / BREAK here;
//              v28–v29 fired at the first green 30s close above the line, still an option)
// Built from the 30s alert's bars; drawn on the candle's own chart.
// 3) (v32–v34's RSI cross and DIP, and v39's MACD cross after a DIP, were here until v44 removed them.)
// 4) EMA CROSS OVER VWAP (v35): the EMA of a timeframe's closes (2m, length 9) crosses above a
// VWAP line (session; month and year are switches), judged at each close of that timeframe's
// candles. Built from a request, so it works on the 2m chart or a smaller one.
//   EMA   above the line at this close, at or under it at the one before
//         (v36) the filter calls a cross weak — its candle opened before 07:00 New York, the EMA
//         was under the line for fewer than 5 candles, or the two crossed more than 2 times in
//         the 20 candles before: drawn gray, sent with `| weak`, not announced
//   BOUNCE (v37) after an EMA cross, a candle's low comes down to the EMA or the VWAP and that
//         candle or a later one closes green above the EMA — the pullback entry, with a stop
//         under the pullback's low; a close under the VWAP first ends the wait
//   (v40) "EMA cross: the line that crosses the VWAP" — EMA, BB upper (the default since v44), or Both.
//         BB upper is the VB's upper Bollinger Band (its BB timeframe, length and StdDev) crossing
//         the VWAP by the same rule, settings and filter, with its own day's numbers; its message
//         carries the band in the EMA's place and the dashboard calls it BAND. The BOUNCE stays
//         the EMA's (section 4b)
//   (v41) a band cross whose candle closed under the band's middle line — the band widened on a
//         fast drop and rose over the VWAP while the price fell away — is weak: gray, `| weak`,
//         not announced (an input; the message carries `| mid` either way)
//   (v42's BASIS cross, the basis of a separate Bollinger Band over the VWAP, was removed in v44.)
// VWAP lines (v28): from 30s bars by default, so the session line is the same on every
// chart (TradingView's built-in VWAP is built from the chart's own bars and differs by
// timeframe), or from the chart's bars ("VWAP lines from" in Inputs).
// Run it as TradingView watchlist alerts — one on 1m and one on 30s (Premium allows 2):
// Symbols = the runners list (dashboard → 📐 sidebar ⋯ → Copy list), session Extended,
// condition = this script → "Any alert() function call", once per bar close,
// webhook = https://pnldash.uz/api/tv/webhook?key=<TV_WEBHOOK_SECRET>.
// The alert message format below is parsed by apps/api/src/services/tv-setups.ts —
// keep the two in step. The offline replica (apps/api/scripts/research/vwap-setup/)
// mirrors this logic; update it with the script.
indicator("mVWAP x BB basis setup", shorttitle = "mVWAP-BB", overlay = true)

// v27 put the inputs in a new order (TradingView keeps saved values by position, so
// after the paste: Settings → Defaults → Reset settings). The defaults were the
// operator's own settings on 10-28: gainer filter 10%, VB candle 5m, band 45s (v44: 2m and 30s).
// From here on, new inputs go last again.
// v39 took inputs out of the middle (the VB lanes) and the end (the LIFT), so it needs the same
// Reset settings once. The RSI's defaults became the operator's (a 10m RSI checked at 1h), so
// the reset lands on their setup.
// v44 took inputs out of the middle again (the RSI's, the DIP's, the MACD's) and the end (the
// BASIS's), so it needs the same Reset settings once. Four defaults became the operator's live
// settings (VB candle 2m, VB band 30S, EMA candle 2m, the EMA cross's line "BB upper"), so the
// reset lands on them.
// Gainer filter: computed per ticker from its own bars — no screener, no ranking.
// A ticker that doesn't pass stays silent; -100 switches the filter off.
minDayGain = input.float(10.0, "Up at least % (day high vs prior close; -100 = filter off)", group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
runnerDays = input.int(3,      "…today, or on any of the last N sessions (0 = today only)", minval = 0, maxval = 5, group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
useAhGain  = input.bool(true,  "After hours, also count the move since today's close", group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
alertWin   = input.session("0400-2000", "Alert window (New York time)", group = "Alerts")
pbOn       = input.bool(true,   "Pullback setup on", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbSession  = input.bool(true,   "Lines: session VWAP", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbMonth    = input.bool(true,   "month VWAP", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbYear     = input.bool(true,   "year VWAP (v14)", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbArm      = input.float(15.0,  "Armed: a bar high at least % above the line (the big move)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbNear     = input.float(5.0,   "PULLBACK: a close back within % above the line", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbLowMY    = input.bool(true,   "Month / year lines: a candle's low reaching the band counts, its close holding above the line (v24 trial)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbBreak    = input.float(0.0,   "BROKEN: a close at least % under the line (0 = any close under it)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbWin      = input.float(10.0,  "HELD: price runs % above the PULLBACK close", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbMax      = input.int(0,       "Script cap: stop a line after N failed pullbacks a day (0 = none; the dashboard applies the cap since v16)", minval = 0, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbCapMark  = input.int(2,       "Chart: pullbacks after N failed ones are drawn gray (the dashboard's cap)", minval = 1, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbTimeout  = input.int(60,      "Stop watching a pullback after N bars", minval = 1, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
vbOn       = input.bool(true,         "VWAP + BB cross setup on (v21)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbCandleTf = input.timeframe("2",     "VB: candle timeframe — the chart you trade (its candles and session VWAP)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbBbTf     = input.timeframe("30S",   "VB: BB timeframe (the band)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbLen      = input.int(20,            "VB: BB length", minval = 2, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbMult     = input.float(2.0,         "VB: BB StdDev", minval = 0.1, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbTol      = input.float(0.0,         "VB: the candle may open up to % above the lower line (price sitting on VWAP; 0 = under both)", minval = 0, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbGainOn   = input.bool(true,         "VB: gainers only (the gainer filter at the top)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbSession  = input.bool(true,         "VB lines: session VWAP", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbMonth    = input.bool(true,         "month VWAP (v22)", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbYear     = input.bool(true,         "year VWAP (v22)", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
// v28: these two kept the VB break's (v25–v27) places, so saved values stay put.
vbRtOn     = input.bool(true,         "VB retest (v28): after the VB candle closes, price back at the line it crossed and a 30s candle closing green above it", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbRtCancel = input.bool(true,         "VB retest: a candle closing back under the VWAP line the VB candle crossed cancels it", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbTf       = input.timeframe("30S",   "VB: alerts from the alert on this chart timeframe (30S = soonest)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbShow     = input.bool(true,         "VB: draw the band and markers (on the candle timeframe's chart)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
// v28 inputs go last.
vwSrc      = input.string("30s bars", "VWAP lines from (v28): 30s bars — the same line on every chart — or the chart's bars (TradingView's built-in)", options = ["30s bars", "Chart bars"], group = "Alerts")
vbRtNear   = input.float(1.0,         "VB retest: price back within % above the line (0 = to the line or under it)", minval = 0, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbRtWait   = input.int(6,             "VB retest: within N candles of the VB candle's close (0 = until cancelled)", minval = 0, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
// (v29's eighteen "VB lanes" inputs sat here until v39 removed the lanes.)
// v30 inputs go last.
vbRtWhen   = input.string("Candle close", "VB retest fires (v30): at the close of the candle that came back to the line, if it closes above it — or at the first green 30s close above it (v28)", options = ["Candle close", "30s bounce"], group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
rtAtClose  = vbRtWhen == "Candle close"
// v31 inputs go last.
mvSrc      = input.string("30s bars", "Month VWAP from (v31): 30s bars — this month's hourly bars + today's 30s bars, one line for every chart and setup — or the chart's bars (TradingView's anchored VWAP)", options = ["30s bars", "Chart bars"], group = "Alerts")
mv30       = mvSrc == "30s bars"

// Same lines as the chart: VWAP anchor Month on hlc3,
// and (v10, PULLBACK) VWAP anchor Session, which resets at timeframe.change("D"),
// the 04:00 ET pre-market open on an Extended chart. Each restarts on the first
// loaded bar too, exactly like TradingView's built-in VWAP
// (`if na(src[1]) … isNewPeriod := true`), so a line never goes blank when its
// anchor isn't in the loaded history (the month line late in a month on 30s).
firstBar = na(hlc3[1])
mvChart = ta.vwap(hlc3, timeframe.change("M") or firstBar)
svChart = ta.vwap(hlc3, timeframe.change("D") or firstBar)

// The year line (v11; v14 builds it from hourly bars). An intraday chart loads
// weeks of history, not a year, so a year VWAP from the chart's own bars started
// wherever the history began and differed by timeframe: SDEV 2026-10-05 was 4.36
// on the 30s chart and 4.70 on the 2m alert. v14 takes this year's 60-minute bars
// (extended hours) up to the end of yesterday, from a request that reaches back
// to January, and adds today's bars from the chart, so the 30s chart, the 1m alert
// and the 30s alert share one line. `anchorsBefore` returns the year's and (v31) the month's sums
// up to the start of the current day; they don't depend on the current hour, which is why
// lookahead_on is safe here.
// v43: THIS MUST STAY THE SCRIPT'S FIRST request.*() CALL. On a 30s chart, a timeframe's bars
// first asked for after a request.security_lower_tf() call load only as deep as 100,000 30s bars
// would reach (833 hourly bars, two to five months; 34 daily bars), and every later request for
// that timeframe shares what the first one loaded. v28 put its 30s-bar request above this one,
// so from 2026-10-29 to v42 the 30s chart's and the 30s alert's year line (and the VB's, which
// asks for the same hourly bars) started months late instead of in January: on the same ticker
// and day it sat a median 21% under the 1m alert's (LXEO 2026-11-18: 3.64 against 4.79; the
// year's VWAP from daily bars is 4.86). Asked for first, the hourly bars load in full and the
// VB's request further down shares them. The month line was not affected.
anchorsBefore() =>
    var float pv     = 0.0
    var float v      = 0.0
    var float pvDay  = 0.0
    var float vDay   = 0.0
    var float mpv    = 0.0
    var float mv     = 0.0
    var float mpvDay = 0.0
    var float mvDay  = 0.0
    if timeframe.change("D")
        pvDay  := pv
        vDay   := v
        mpvDay := mpv
        mvDay  := mv
    if timeframe.change("M")
        mpv    := 0.0
        mv     := 0.0
        mpvDay := 0.0
        mvDay  := 0.0
    if timeframe.change("12M")
        pv    := 0.0
        v     := 0.0
        pvDay := 0.0
        vDay  := 0.0
    pv  := pv + hlc3 * volume
    v   := v + volume
    mpv := mpv + hlc3 * volume
    mv  := mv + volume
    [pvDay, vDay, mpvDay, mvDay]
[yPrevPV, yPrevV, mPrevPV, mPrevV] = request.security(ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended), "60", anchorsBefore(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)

// v28 (operator, 10-29: "vwaps in tv chart are differs for 5min and 30s"): a VWAP built
// from bars counts each bar's volume at the bar's (high + low + close) / 3, so bigger bars
// drift further from the true VWAP. On the operator's alerts since 10-23 the 5m-candle
// line sat a median 0.4% from the 30s chart's (90% within 0.9%) and the 10m one 1.6%
// (90% within 4.9%); the 1m one 0.07%. "30s bars" (the default) builds the session line,
// and today's part of the year line, from the 30s bars inside each chart bar, so every
// chart shows one line, closer to the true VWAP (and to our research's). Charts of 30s or
// less use their own bars. "Chart bars" = TradingView's built-in, as before v28. v28 left the
// month line as the chart's anchored VWAP ("most of its volume is from earlier days"); on a name
// whose one day dwarfs the month that's wrong — ROMA 10-28: the 1h chart drew ~5.94, the 30s / 1m
// alerts ~6.35, and the VB used its own line — so v31 gives the month line its own switch (below).
use30   = vwSrc == "30s bars"
chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
lower30 = use30 and chartSec > 30
need30  = (use30 or mv30) and chartSec > 30   // v31: the month line can want 30s bars on its own
[w30PV, w30V] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, need30 ? "30S" : timeframe.period, [hlc3 * volume, volume])
float barPV = 0.0
float barV  = 0.0
int   w30N  = array.size(w30PV)
if w30N > 0
    for i = 0 to w30N - 1
        barPV := barPV + nz(array.get(w30PV, i))
        barV  := barV + nz(array.get(w30V, i))
var float s30PV = 0.0
var float s30V  = 0.0
if timeframe.change("D") or firstBar
    s30PV := 0.0
    s30V  := 0.0
s30PV := s30PV + barPV
s30V  := s30V + barV
svwap = lower30 ? (s30V > 0 ? s30PV / s30V : na) : svChart

// Today's part of the year line; the days before today come from anchorsBefore(), requested
// above the 30s-bar request (v43: it must be the script's first request).
var float yDayPV = 0.0
var float yDayV  = 0.0
if timeframe.change("D")
    yDayPV := 0.0
    yDayV  := 0.0
yDayPV := yDayPV + (lower30 ? barPV : hlc3 * volume)
yDayV  := yDayV + (lower30 ? barV : volume)
yvwap = na(yPrevV) or yPrevV + yDayV <= 0 ? na : (yPrevPV + yDayPV) / (yPrevV + yDayV)
// v31 "Month VWAP from: 30s bars" (the default): this month's hourly bars before today + today's
// 30s bars (the chart's own on charts of 30s or less) — the line the VB has used since v28, now also
// the one drawn and the one PULLBACK uses, the same on every chart. "Chart bars": the chart's
// anchored VWAP, as before v31 (the VB keeps its hourly-based line either way).
mvwap = mv30 ? (na(mPrevV) or mPrevV + s30V <= 0 ? na : (mPrevPV + s30PV) / (mPrevV + s30V)) : mvChart
// Strength inputs sent with every signal (v9): the signal bar's volume vs the
// average of the previous 20 bars, and the run-up over the previous 10 bars.
// PULLBACK messages carry them; the server stores them for grading.
volAvg20 = ta.sma(volume, 20)[1]
volX     = volAvg20 > 0 ? volume / volAvg20 : na
runUp10  = (close / close[10] - 1) * 100
// v21: a line is drawn while a setup that uses it is on.
plot((pbOn and pbMonth) or (vbOn and vbMonth) ? mvwap : na, "mVWAP", color.yellow)
plot((pbOn and pbSession) or (vbOn and vbSession) ? svwap : na, "sVWAP", color.purple)
plot((pbOn and pbYear) or (vbOn and vbYear) ? yvwap : na, "yVWAP", color.blue)

// Top gainer: today's high vs the prior regular-session close (like Finviz
// Change), or the same in any of the last `runnerDays` sessions — a second- or
// third-day runner sets up BEFORE it is up on the day (MEDS 2026-09-18) — or,
// after hours, the high since today's close (Finviz's AH change: AMOD fell 24%
// on 2026-10-01, then ran +70% after hours from a +19.8% day high).
newDay = timeframe.change("D")
var float lastRegClose = na
var float prevDayClose = na
var float dayHigh      = na
var dayGains = array.new<float>()   // day-high gains of finished sessions, newest first (max 5)
var float ahHigh       = na   // high since today's close (post-market bars)
if newDay
    array.unshift(dayGains, (dayHigh / prevDayClose - 1) * 100)
    if array.size(dayGains) > 5
        array.pop(dayGains)
    prevDayClose := lastRegClose
    dayHigh      := high
    ahHigh       := na
else
    dayHigh := na(dayHigh) ? high : math.max(dayHigh, high)
if session.ismarket
    lastRegClose := close
if session.ispostmarket
    ahHigh := na(ahHigh) ? high : math.max(ahHigh, high)
ahGain = session.ispostmarket and not na(ahHigh) ? (ahHigh / lastRegClose - 1) * 100 : na
dayHighGain = (dayHigh / prevDayClose - 1) * 100
float recentGain = -100.0
lookback = math.min(runnerDays, array.size(dayGains))
if lookback > 0
    for i = 0 to lookback - 1
        g = array.get(dayGains, i)
        if not na(g)
            recentGain := math.max(recentGain, g)
gainer = (not na(dayHighGain) and dayHighGain >= minDayGain) or recentGain >= minDayGain or
     (useAhGain and not na(ahGain) and ahGain >= minDayGain)

inWindow = not na(time(timeframe.period, alertWin, "America/New_York"))

pctVs(float ln) => (close >= ln ? "+" : "") + str.tostring((close / ln - 1) * 100, "#.0")

// ── 1) PULLBACK (v10) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A fast run stretches price well above a VWAP line and it comes back down to it
// (operator, 2026-10-05: SAIQ and SDEV on the session line, VEEA 2026-09-15 on
// the month line, MI 2026-10-05 12:40 ET on the year line). Each line keeps its
// own state, reset every day:
//   armed     by a bar high ≥ pbArm% above the line (gainers only)
//   PULLBACK  on a LATER close within pbNear% above the line ("be ready")
//   BROKEN    then a close pbBreak% under the line — the operator's exit — or
//   HELD      a high +pbWin% above the PULLBACK close, whichever comes first;
//             after pbTimeout bars the pullback is dropped silently.
// A close straight through the line while armed is a touch with no PULLBACK.
// Re-arming needs a new bar high ≥ pbArm% above the line. v15: the day's cap
// (pbMax) counts FAILED pullbacks — BROKEN or straight through — not every touch.
// A line that keeps holding keeps alerting (MI 2026-10-05: six year-line touches,
// every alerted one HELD, but v14's 2-touch cap blocked 11:44, 12:37 and 12:57);
// a line that failed twice stops. Four months of session-line data: at least as good
// on every exit rule, ~2 more alerts a day (docs/vwap-setup.md §13.5).
// v16 (2026-10-10): the cap moved to the dashboard. The script alerts every
// pullback (pbMax 0) and each PULLBACK says how many failed before it on its line
// (`fails N`); the server stays quiet past 2 failures unless the ticker is on our
// Momentum list at grade B+ or better (WFF 10-09: a year-line pullback ran +40%
// past the cap). Cap tweaks no longer need a new script or new alerts.
type PbLine
    bool  armed    = false
    int   armBar   = na
    float peakPct  = na
    int   touches  = 0
    int   fails    = 0
    bool  open     = false
    float entry    = na
    int   alertBar = na

// One bar of one line's setup: 0 nothing, 1 PULLBACK, 2 BROKEN, 3 HELD.
// v24 (operator, RBNE 10-21 04:10 ET: the dip tagged the month line's band with its
// low, ~1.20 over a ~1.17 line, but closed 7–8% above it, then ran to 1.92): `useLow`
// lets the bar's low reach the band, the close still at or above the line. A trial on
// the month and year lines only — on four months of the session line (research/
// vwap-pullback --touch low) the low added ~2 alerts a day at 0.3–0.9 points worse a
// trade, and the month and year lines can only be graded live. Such a PULLBACK's
// message shows its close more than pbNear % above the line.
method step(PbLine s, float ln, bool canArm, bool useLow) =>
    int ev = 0
    if not na(ln) and ln > 0
        if s.open
            if close < ln * (1 - pbBreak / 100)
                s.open  := false
                s.fails := s.fails + 1
                ev := 2
            else if high >= s.entry * (1 + pbWin / 100)
                s.open := false
                ev := 3
            else if bar_index - s.alertBar >= pbTimeout
                s.open := false
        if not s.open
            float stretch = (high / ln - 1) * 100
            if not s.armed
                if canArm and stretch >= pbArm
                    s.armed   := true
                    s.armBar  := bar_index
                    s.peakPct := stretch
            else
                s.peakPct := math.max(s.peakPct, stretch)
                float reach = useLow ? low : close
                if bar_index > s.armBar and reach <= ln * (1 + pbNear / 100)
                    s.armed   := false
                    s.touches := s.touches + 1
                    if close < ln * (1 - pbBreak / 100)
                        s.fails := s.fails + 1
                    else if ev == 0 and (pbMax == 0 or s.fails < pbMax)
                        s.open     := true
                        s.entry    := close
                        s.alertBar := bar_index
                        ev := 1
    ev

var PbLine pbS = PbLine.new()
var PbLine pbM = PbLine.new()
var PbLine pbY = PbLine.new()
if newDay
    pbS.armed   := false
    pbS.open    := false
    pbS.touches := 0
    pbS.fails   := 0
    pbM.armed   := false
    pbM.open    := false
    pbM.touches := 0
    pbM.fails   := 0
    pbY.armed   := false
    pbY.open    := false
    pbY.touches := 0
    pbY.fails   := 0
int evS = 0
int evM = 0
int evY = 0
if pbOn and inWindow
    if pbSession
        evS := pbS.step(svwap, gainer, false)
    if pbMonth
        evM := pbM.step(mvwap, gainer, pbLowMY)
    if pbYear
        evY := pbY.step(yvwap, gainer, pbLowMY)

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage:
//   PULLBACK SAIQ 6.2 | sVWAP 6.16 (+0.7%) | mVWAP 4.1 (+51.2%) | line session | touch 2 | fails 0 | peak +17% | day high +336% | vol 0.6x | run -9.6% | tf 1
// v16: `fails` = failed pullbacks on the line before this one (the lowest of the lines named).
pbMsg(int ev, string lineName, int touch, float peak, int fails) =>
    string msg = (ev == 1 ? "PULLBACK" : ev == 2 ? "BROKEN" : "HELD") + " " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(svwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(svwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(mvwap) + "%)"
    if not na(yvwap)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(yvwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | line " + lineName + " | touch " + str.tostring(touch)
    if ev == 1
        msg += " | fails " + str.tostring(fails)
    if ev == 1 and not na(peak)
        msg += " | peak +" + str.tostring(peak, "#") + "%"
    msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(volX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(volX, "#.#") + "x"
    if not na(runUp10)
        msg += " | run " + (runUp10 >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(runUp10, "#.#") + "%"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

// Lines firing the same event on one bar (they sit close together early in a
// month) are one message naming all of them, e.g. "line session+month" (v10–v13
// said "both" for session + month): the lowest touch number and failure count, the highest peak.
pbJoin(string acc, string name) => acc == "" ? name : acc + "+" + name
pbFire(int e) =>
    string names = ""
    int touch = 999
    int fails = 999
    float peak = na
    if evS == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbS.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbS.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbS.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbS.peakPct, peak))
    if evM == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbM.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbM.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbM.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbM.peakPct, peak))
    if evY == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbY.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbY.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbY.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbY.peakPct, peak))
    [names, touch, peak, fails]

[pbN1, pbT1, pbP1, pbF1] = pbFire(1)
[pbN2, pbT2, pbP2, pbF2] = pbFire(2)
[pbN3, pbT3, pbP3, pbF3] = pbFire(3)
if pbN1 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(1, pbN1, pbT1, pbP1, pbF1), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if pbN2 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(2, pbN2, pbT2, pbP2, pbF2), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if pbN3 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(3, pbN3, pbT3, pbP3, pbF3), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// v16: a pullback past the dashboard's cap (pbCapMark failures on every line it names)
// is drawn gray — it only pings for a B+-or-better ticker on our Momentum list.
bool pbCapped = pbN1 != "" and pbF1 >= pbCapMark
plotshape(pbN1 != "" and not pbCapped, "Pullback", shape.diamond, location.belowbar, color.aqua, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(pbCapped, "Pullback (past the cap)", shape.diamond, location.belowbar, color.gray, size = size.tiny)
// v28: BROKEN and HELD are hidden by default (the operator hides them); Style can show them.
plotshape(evS == 2 or evM == 2 or evY == 2, "Broken", shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.red, size = size.tiny, display = display.none)
plotshape(evS == 3 or evM == 3 or evY == 3, "Held", shape.flag, location.abovebar, color.lime, size = size.tiny, display = display.none)

// ── 2) VWAP + BB CROSS (v21; v22 adds the month and year lines) ───────────────
// The operator's fourth setup (2026-10-20; AIXI, WORX and NWGL on 5m charts): "the
// market is colder than before, and it's very hard to trade with 1min timeframe".
// On a chart of their choice (5m, 1h, …) with its session VWAP and the upper
// Bollinger Band of another timeframe (2m on the 5m chart; 30m or 45m on the 1h
// chart), one candle crosses over both lines. They want the alert at that moment,
// not at the candle's close. v22 (operator: "it's ok to add a support for month and
// year"): the same rule on the month and the year VWAP, each line with its own state.
//   CROSS  at a 30s close inside the candle, its open is at or under both the line and
//          the band as they stand then (at most vbTol % over the lower one: price
//          sitting on the line counts) and the close is above both → the alert; once
//          per candle and line. v23 (operator, WHLR 10-21 04:00 ET: "this one
//          definitely should be considered as a VB … if 1 candle crosses both vwap and
//          bb upper row"): the lines as they stand at that close — what the chart
//          draws for the candle — not as they stood when it opened, and the day's
//          first candle counts. A 04:00 gap-and-go (WHLR 0.36 → open 0.43 → 0.55)
//          drags its own VWAP and band above its open; v21/v22 saw an open above
//          yesterday's lines and stayed silent.
// Premium's two watchlist-alert slots are taken (1m + 30s), so it rides the 30s alert
// (like v17–v26's breakout): vbStep() builds the candle, its VWAP lines and the band (SMA /
// StdDev of the BB timeframe's closes, the forming one live) from the 30s bars. The
// session line is the candle timeframe's own (hlc3 × volume of its candles). A 30s
// chart doesn't hold a month of history, so the month and year lines take the days
// before today from this year's hourly bars (vbAnchors(), like the year line since
// v14) and add today's candles. The candle's chart replays the same 30s bars
// (request.security_lower_tf), so its markers are the alerts. Gainers only by
// default: the filter at the top, recomputed from the 30s bars
// (a request can't read the chart's running values). Lines firing on one 30s bar are
// one message (`line session+month`); `cross N` counts the day's crosses on each line
// (the lowest of the lines named), and the server announces the first few
// (TV_SETUP.vb_cap).
vbOk  = vbOn and timeframe.in_seconds(vbCandleTf) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf) and timeframe.in_seconds(vbBbTf) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)

// The month's and the year's Σ hlc3 × volume and Σ volume up to the start of the
// current day, on hourly bars (extended hours). They don't depend on the current
// hour, which is why lookahead_on is safe here (as in anchorsBefore()).
vbAnchors() =>
    var float aMPV  = 0.0
    var float aMV   = 0.0
    var float aYPV  = 0.0
    var float aYV   = 0.0
    var float aMPVd = 0.0
    var float aMVd  = 0.0
    var float aYPVd = 0.0
    var float aYVd  = 0.0
    bool aNewDay   = timeframe.change("D")
    bool aNewMonth = timeframe.change("M")
    bool aNewYear  = timeframe.change("12M")
    if aNewDay
        aMPVd := aMPV
        aMVd  := aMV
        aYPVd := aYPV
        aYVd  := aYV
    if aNewMonth
        aMPV  := 0.0
        aMV   := 0.0
        aMPVd := 0.0
        aMVd  := 0.0
    if aNewYear
        aYPV  := 0.0
        aYV   := 0.0
        aYPVd := 0.0
        aYVd  := 0.0
    aMPV := aMPV + hlc3 * volume
    aMV  := aMV + volume
    aYPV := aYPV + hlc3 * volume
    aYV  := aYV + volume
    [aMPVd, aMVd, aYPVd, aYVd]

// One line's CROSS test, on the line and the band as they stand now (v23): the candle's
// open is at or under the higher of them and at most vbTol % over the lower one, and
// the close is above both — the candle's body crosses both.
vbCan(float ln, float up, float cOpen, bool fired) =>
    not fired and not na(ln) and not na(up) and cOpen <= math.max(ln, up) and cOpen <= math.min(ln, up) * (1 + vbTol / 100) and close > ln and close > up

// v26: the lowest of the VWAP lines a VB candle crossed (session / month / year), na if none is known.
vbLowest(bool onS, bool onM, bool onY, float lnS, float lnM, float lnY) =>
    float lowLn = na
    if onS and not na(lnS)
        lowLn := lnS
    if onM and not na(lnM)
        lowLn := na(lowLn) ? lnM : math.min(lowLn, lnM)
    if onY and not na(lnY)
        lowLn := na(lowLn) ? lnY : math.min(lowLn, lnY)
    lowLn

// v28: the highest of them — the first line a pullback reaches, the one the retest watches.
vbHighest(bool onS, bool onM, bool onY, float lnS, float lnM, float lnY) =>
    float hiLn = na
    if onS and not na(lnS)
        hiLn := lnS
    if onM and not na(lnM)
        hiLn := na(hiLn) ? lnM : math.max(hiLn, lnM)
    if onY and not na(lnY)
        hiLn := na(hiLn) ? lnY : math.max(hiLn, lnY)
    hiLn

// The VB's state machine: the candle and band timeframes, its lines, and whether it is on (and
// valid against the alert timeframe). Each call has its own state: one for the alert, one inside
// the chart's replay. (v29–v38 also called it once per "lane", three more candle timeframes.)
vbStep(simple string cTf, simple string bTf, bool onS, bool onM, bool onY, bool laneOk) =>
    // Called on every bar: and/or are lazy in v6, so the timeframe tests and the
    // request come first.
    bool gNewDay   = timeframe.change("D")
    bool vNewBb    = timeframe.change(bTf)
    bool vNewCndl  = timeframe.change(cTf)
    bool vCarry    = timeframe.in_seconds(cTf) >= 14400   // v29: 4h+ candles carry a month / year retest overnight
    bool vEndsNow  = time_close == time_close(cTf)        // v30: this bar closes the candle
    bool vInWin    = not na(time(timeframe.period, alertWin, "America/New_York"))
    [vMBPV, vMBV, vYBPV, vYBV] = request.security(ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended), "60", vbAnchors(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
    // The gainer filter, as at the top of the script.
    var float gLastReg = na
    var float gPrev    = na
    var float gHigh    = na
    var float gAhHigh  = na
    var gGains = array.new<float>()   // finished sessions' day-high gains, newest first (max 5)
    if gNewDay
        array.unshift(gGains, (gHigh / gPrev - 1) * 100)
        if array.size(gGains) > 5
            array.pop(gGains)
        gPrev   := gLastReg
        gHigh   := high
        gAhHigh := na
    else
        gHigh := na(gHigh) ? high : math.max(gHigh, high)
    if session.ismarket
        gLastReg := close
    if session.ispostmarket
        gAhHigh := na(gAhHigh) ? high : math.max(gAhHigh, high)
    float gAh     = session.ispostmarket and not na(gAhHigh) ? (gAhHigh / gLastReg - 1) * 100 : na
    float gDay    = (gHigh / gPrev - 1) * 100
    float gRecent = -100.0
    int   gLook   = math.min(runnerDays, array.size(gGains))
    if gLook > 0
        for i = 0 to gLook - 1
            float gOne = array.get(gGains, i)
            if not na(gOne)
                gRecent := math.max(gRecent, gOne)
    bool gOk = (not na(gDay) and gDay >= minDayGain) or gRecent >= minDayGain or (useAhGain and not na(gAh) and gAh >= minDayGain)
    // The band: the BB timeframe's last vbLen - 1 finished closes plus the forming one.
    var vCloses = array.new<float>()
    var float vLastC = na
    if vNewBb and not na(vLastC)
        array.push(vCloses, vLastC)
        if array.size(vCloses) > vbLen - 1
            array.shift(vCloses)
    vLastC := close
    float vBand = na
    int   vN    = array.size(vCloses)
    if vN == vbLen - 1
        float vSum = close
        for i = 0 to vN - 1
            vSum := vSum + array.get(vCloses, i)
        float vMean = vSum / vbLen
        float vSq   = math.pow(close - vMean, 2)
        for i = 0 to vN - 1
            vSq := vSq + math.pow(array.get(vCloses, i) - vMean, 2)
        vBand := vMean + vbMult * math.sqrt(vSq / vbLen)
    // The candle, and the day's Σ over its finished candles.
    var float vPV      = 0.0     // Σ hlc3 × volume…
    var float vV       = 0.0     // …and Σ volume
    var float vOpen    = na
    var float vHigh    = na
    var float vLow     = na
    var float vClose   = na
    var float vVol     = 0.0
    var bool  vSFired  = false
    var bool  vMFired  = false
    var bool  vYFired  = false
    var int   vSCount  = 0
    var int   vMCount  = 0
    var int   vYCount  = 0
    var vVols = array.new<float>()   // the last 20 finished candles' volumes
    // v28: the latest VB candle's retest — the lines it crossed, whether price has come back to
    // the line yet, the pullback's low, and the candles since the VB candle closed.
    var bool  vRtS     = false
    var bool  vRtM     = false
    var bool  vRtY     = false
    var bool  vRtArmed = false
    var bool  vRtTouch = false
    var float vRtLow   = na
    var int   vRtAge   = 0
    var int   vRtCount = 0
    var float vPrevVw  = na     // v26: the last bar's lines (where they stood at the candle's close)
    var float vPrevMw  = na
    var float vPrevYw  = na
    var float vPV30    = 0.0    // v28: today's Σ hlc3 × volume and Σ volume over the 30s bars
    var float vV30     = 0.0
    var bool  vEndSeen = false  // v30: the forming candle's closing bar has been judged
    bool  vRt     = false
    bool  vRtLate = false       // v31: judged on the next candle's first bar (its closing bar had no trades)
    float vRtStop = na
    float vRtPx   = na          // v30: the RETEST's price — the candle's close (with "Candle close")
    if gNewDay or vNewCndl or na(vOpen)
        // v30: a candle whose closing 30s bar had no trades is judged here, on its last bar's values
        // (30 s late); normally the candle's own closing bar judges it (below).
        if rtAtClose and vRtArmed and vRtTouch and not vEndSeen and not na(vOpen)
            float vLnE = vbHighest(vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vPrevVw, vPrevMw, vPrevYw)
            if not na(vLnE) and vClose > vLnE and vInWin
                vRtArmed := false
                vRt      := true
                vRtStop  := vRtLow - syminfo.mintick
                vRtPx    := vClose
                vRtLate  := true
                vRtCount := vRtCount + 1
        vEndSeen := false
        // The candle that just closed (its values are still here): a VB candle arms a retest,
        // replacing the last one. A new day clears it — except (v29) on a lane of 4h or longer
        // candles, where a retest of the month / year lines carries over (a 4h candle closing at
        // 20:00, a daily one); one involving the session line still ends with the session.
        if gNewDay
            vRtCount := 0
            if vRtArmed and (vRtS or not vCarry)
                vRtArmed := false
        if vbRtOn and not na(vOpen) and (vSFired or vMFired or vYFired) and not (gNewDay and (vSFired or not vCarry))
            vRtS     := vSFired
            vRtM     := vMFired
            vRtY     := vYFired
            vRtArmed := true
            vRtTouch := false
            vRtLow   := na
            vRtAge   := 0
        else if vRtArmed and not na(vOpen)
            vRtAge := vRtAge + 1
        // v26: that candle — the VB candle itself or a later one — closed under the lowest line the
        // VB candle crossed: the retest is off. So is one past vbRtWait candles.
        if vbRtCancel and vRtArmed and not na(vOpen)
            float vLnC = vbLowest(vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vPrevVw, vPrevMw, vPrevYw)
            if not na(vLnC) and vClose < vLnC
                vRtArmed := false
        if vRtArmed and vbRtWait > 0 and vRtAge >= vbRtWait
            vRtArmed := false
        if not na(vOpen)
            array.push(vVols, vVol)
            if array.size(vVols) > 20
                array.shift(vVols)
        if gNewDay
            vPV     := 0.0
            vV      := 0.0
            vSCount := 0
            vMCount := 0
            vYCount := 0
        else if not na(vOpen)
            vPV := vPV + (vHigh + vLow + vClose) / 3 * vVol
            vV  := vV + vVol
        vOpen    := open
        vHigh    := high
        vLow     := low
        vVol     := volume
        vSFired  := false
        vMFired  := false
        vYFired  := false
    else
        vHigh := math.max(vHigh, high)
        vLow  := math.min(vLow, low)
        vVol  := vVol + volume
    vClose := close
    if gNewDay
        vPV30 := 0.0
        vV30  := 0.0
    vPV30 := vPV30 + hlc3 * volume
    vV30  := vV30 + volume
    // Today's part of the lines: the candles' (hlc3 × volume of each candle, the forming one
    // included — the candle chart's built-in VWAP) or, with "30s bars" (v28), the 30s bars'.
    float vTPV    = use30 ? vPV30 : vPV + (vHigh + vLow + close) / 3 * vVol
    float vTV     = use30 ? vV30 : vV + vVol
    float vVw     = vTV > 0 ? vTPV / vTV : na
    float vMPV    = mv30 ? vPV30 : vTPV    // v31: the month line's today, per its own switch
    float vMV     = mv30 ? vV30 : vTV
    float vMw     = not na(vMBV) and vMBV + vMV > 0 ? (vMBPV + vMPV) / (vMBV + vMV) : na
    float vYw     = not na(vYBV) and vYBV + vTV > 0 ? (vYBPV + vTPV) / (vYBV + vTV) : na
    float vAvgVol = array.size(vVols) > 0 ? array.avg(vVols) : na
    float vVolX   = not na(vAvgVol) and vAvgVol > 0 ? vVol / vAvgVol : na
    bool  vOkAll  = laneOk and vInWin and (not vbGainOn or gOk)
    bool  vFireS  = vOkAll and onS and vbCan(vVw, vBand, vOpen, vSFired)
    bool  vFireM  = vOkAll and onM and vbCan(vMw, vBand, vOpen, vMFired)
    bool  vFireY  = vOkAll and onY and vbCan(vYw, vBand, vOpen, vYFired)
    if vFireS
        vSFired := true
        vSCount := vSCount + 1
    if vFireM
        vMFired := true
        vMCount := vMCount + 1
    if vFireY
        vYFired := true
        vYCount := vYCount + 1
    // v28 RETEST (the operator's entry): from the first bar after the VB candle closed, a bar whose
    // low comes within vbRtNear % above the highest line the VB candle crossed (or under it), then
    // the first bar from there that closes above that line and above its own open — the bounce.
    // The stop is a tick under the pullback's low (the lowest low since the VB candle closed).
    // Measured (research/vwap-bb-cross/vb_retest_study.py, 5m candles, 06-12 → 10-28): −0.92% a
    // trade against −1.26% for the v25 break and −1.87% for the CROSS, a 2.2% median stop, 22%
    // reaching 2R first; per unit of risk the break did better (−0.14R vs −0.30R). A heads-up.
    // v30 (operator, CLPT 10-29: "RT should not be fired if its candle's close is under the vwap"):
    // with "Candle close" (the default) the RETEST waits for the close of the candle that came back to
    // the line and fires only if that candle closes above it; a close under the lowest crossed line
    // cancels it (above). Measured (vb_retest_study.py, 5m / 10m, 06-12 → 10-28): −0.84% / −0.83% a
    // trade vs −0.92% / −0.91% at the 30s bounce, −0.26R / −0.18R vs −0.31R / −0.25R (stops ≥ 0.5%),
    // stopped 57% vs 63%; also requiring a green candle was worse (−1.44% / −1.21%).
    float vRtLine = vbHighest(vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vVw, vMw, vYw)
    if vRtArmed
        vRtLow := na(vRtLow) ? low : math.min(vRtLow, low)
        if not vRtTouch and not na(vRtLine) and low <= vRtLine * (1 + vbRtNear / 100)
            vRtTouch := true
        bool vRtGo = rtAtClose ? vEndsNow and close > vRtLine : close > vRtLine and close > open
        if vRtTouch and vInWin and not na(vRtLine) and vRtGo
            vRtArmed := false
            vRt      := true
            vRtStop  := vRtLow - syminfo.mintick
            vRtPx    := close
            vRtCount := vRtCount + 1
    if vEndsNow
        vEndSeen := true
    vPrevVw := vVw
    vPrevMw := vMw
    vPrevYw := vYw
    [vFireS, vFireM, vFireY, vVw, vMw, vYw, vBand, vOpen, gDay, gAh, vVolX, vSCount, vMCount, vYCount, vRt, vRtStop, vRtS, vRtM, vRtY, vRtCount, vRtPx, vRtLate]

// On the alert's own chart (30s): the alert, and its markers there (the main VB's).
[vbFireS, vbFireM, vbFireY, vbVw, vbMw, vbYw, vbBand, vbOpen, vbDayG, vbAhG, vbVolX, vbNS, vbNM, vbNY, vbRt, vbRtStop, vbRtS, vbRtM, vbRtY, vbRtN, vbRtPx, vbRtLate] = vbStep(vbCandleTf, vbBbTf, vbSession, vbMonth, vbYear, vbOk)
// On the candle timeframe's chart: the same 30s bars inside each candle, replayed, so its markers
// are the alerts. (v29–v38 chose here which lane's candle timeframe the chart was.)
vbView() =>
    [vwS, vwM, vwY, vwVw, vwMw, vwYw, vwBand, vwOpen, vwDayG, vwAhG, vwVolX, vwNS, vwNM, vwNY, vwRt, vwRtStop, vwRtS, vwRtM, vwRtY, vwRtN, vwRtPx, vwRtLate] = vbStep(vbCandleTf, vbBbTf, vbSession, vbMonth, vbYear, vbOk)
    [vwS, vwM, vwY, vwBand, vwRt and not vwRtLate, vwRt and vwRtLate]
vbBaseSec  = timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)
vbChartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
vbLower    = vbOk and vbShow and timeframe.period == vbCandleTf and vbChartSec > vbBaseSec
[vbInS, vbInM, vbInY, vbInUp, vbInRt, vbInRtL] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, vbLower ? vbTf : timeframe.period, vbView())
bool  vbMarkS = false
bool  vbMarkM = false
bool  vbMarkY = false
bool  vbMarkR = false
bool  vbMarkRL = false   // v31: a late RETEST, drawn on the candle before (the one that closed above the line)
float vbUp    = na
if vbLower
    int vbIn = array.size(vbInS)
    if vbIn > 0
        vbUp := array.get(vbInUp, vbIn - 1)   // the band at the candle's last 30s close
        for k = 0 to vbIn - 1
            if array.get(vbInS, k)
                vbMarkS := true
            if array.get(vbInM, k)
                vbMarkM := true
            if array.get(vbInY, k)
                vbMarkY := true
            if array.get(vbInRt, k)
                vbMarkR := true
            if array.get(vbInRtL, k)
                vbMarkRL := true
else if vbOk and vbShow and vbChartSec == vbBaseSec
    vbMarkS := vbFireS
    vbMarkM := vbFireM
    vbMarkY := vbFireY
    vbMarkR  := vbRt and not vbRtLate
    vbMarkRL := vbRt and vbRtLate
    vbUp     := vbBand

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage. The VWAPs are
// the setup's lines (the candle timeframe's session VWAP, the hourly-anchored month
// and year VWAPs), upper the BB timeframe's band, open the candle's:
//   CROSS AIXI 2.61 | sVWAP 2.47 (+5.7%) | mVWAP 2.55 (+2.4%) | yVWAP 3.1 (-15.8%) | upper 2.58 (+1.2%) | open 2.5 | line session+month | candle 5 | bb 2 | cross 1 | day high +25% | vol 1.8x | tf 30S
vbSend  = vbOk and timeframe.period == vbTf
// The message builder takes the VB's values as arguments (v29 wrote it so for its lanes).
vbMsg(bool lFS, bool lFM, bool lFY, int lNS, int lNM, int lNY, float lVw, float lMw, float lYw, float lBand, float lOpen, float lDayG, float lAhG, float lVolX, string lCTf, string lBTf) =>
    string names = ""
    int    n     = 999
    if lFS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
        n     := math.min(n, lNS)
    if lFM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
        n     := math.min(n, lNM)
    if lFY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
        n     := math.min(n, lNY)
    string msg = "CROSS " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    if not na(lVw)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(lVw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lVw) + "%)"
    if not na(lMw)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(lMw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lMw) + "%)"
    if not na(lYw)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(lYw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lYw) + "%)"
    msg += " | upper " + str.tostring(lBand, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lBand) + "%)"
    msg += " | open " + str.tostring(lOpen, format.mintick)
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + lCTf + " | bb " + lBTf + " | cross " + str.tostring(n)
    if not na(lDayG)
        msg += " | day high " + (lDayG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lDayG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(lAhG)
        msg += " | ah " + (lAhG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lAhG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(lVolX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(lVolX, "#.#") + "x"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

if vbSend and (vbFireS or vbFireM or vbFireY)
    alert(vbMsg(vbFireS, vbFireM, vbFireY, vbNS, vbNM, vbNY, vbVw, vbMw, vbYw, vbBand, vbOpen, vbDayG, vbAhG, vbVolX, vbCandleTf, vbBbTf), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// v28 RETEST (operator, AIOK 10-28/29: "I'm not using BREAKs for enter (because they can be very
// extended by the moment entering), but waiting 1st 5min candle closes with VB and pulls back to
// vwap line and bounces, I'm entering right at that moment"). It replaces v25–v27's LEVEL / BREAK;
// `retest N` counts the day's retests on the ticker, and the server caps them.
//   RETEST AIOK 17.28 | stop 17.09 | sVWAP 17.1 (+1.1%) | mVWAP 14.2 (+21.7%) | line session | candle 5 | bb 45S | retest 1 | day high +46% | vwap 30s | tf 30S
vbRtMsg(bool lRS, bool lRM, bool lRY, float lStop, float lVw, float lMw, float lYw, int lRN, float lDayG, float lAhG, string lCTf, string lBTf, float lPx) =>
    string names = ""
    if lRS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
    if lRM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
    if lRY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
    string msg = "RETEST " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(na(lPx) ? close : lPx, format.mintick)
    msg += " | stop " + str.tostring(lStop, format.mintick)
    if not na(lVw)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(lVw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lVw) + "%)"
    if not na(lMw)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(lMw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lMw) + "%)"
    if not na(lYw)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(lYw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(lYw) + "%)"
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + lCTf + " | bb " + lBTf + " | retest " + str.tostring(lRN)
    if not na(lDayG)
        msg += " | day high " + (lDayG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lDayG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(lAhG)
        msg += " | ah " + (lAhG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(lAhG, "#") + "%"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

if vbSend and vbRt
    alert(vbRtMsg(vbRtS, vbRtM, vbRtY, vbRtStop, vbVw, vbMw, vbYw, vbRtN, vbDayG, vbAhG, vbCandleTf, vbBbTf, vbRtPx), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plot(vbShow and (vbLower or (vbOk and vbChartSec == vbBaseSec)) ? vbUp : na, "BB upper (VWAP + BB cross)", color.new(color.orange, 20))
// v22: the marker says which line crossed (the year's, then the month's, first): teal
// for the session line, yellow "VB M" for the month line, blue "VB Y" for the year line.
plotshape(vbMarkS and not vbMarkM and not vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (session)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.teal, text = "VB", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkM and not vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (month, v22)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.yellow, text = "VB M", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (year, v22)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.blue, text = "VB Y", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkR, "VB retest (v28)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "RT", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
// v31: a RETEST judged on the next bar (its candle's closing 30s bar had no trades) is drawn on that
// candle, one bar back — ROMA 1h 10-28 drew one on the candle after. Its own plot (last in the list);
// give it the same style as "VB retest (v28)" in Style if you restyled that one.
plotshape(vbMarkRL, "VB retest, late close (v31)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "RT", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small, offset = -1)

// (v32–v34's RSI cross and DIP, section 3, sat here until v44 removed them.)
// (v32's seven RSI inputs and v34's three DIP inputs, rsOn … rsDipMax, sat here until v44 removed them.)

// ── 4) EMA CROSS OVER VWAP (v35) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// Operator, 2026-11-13: "I want to be notified when ema crosses up the vwap (for example, 9 ema
// crosses up the session vwap in 3 min chart timeframe)". The EMA of a timeframe's closes against
// a VWAP line, judged at each close of that timeframe's candles: above the line now, at or under
// it at the close before. A request returns the EMA after the last finished candle
// (lookahead on + [1]) and the bar's close makes it live, so it works on any chart whose bars
// divide the timeframe and sends from the 30s alert. The lines are the script's own (the session
// line from 30s bars by default), the ones it draws.
// A candle whose closing bar had no trades is judged on the next bar (`| late`), except across the
// day's end: yesterday's last candle is not announced this morning (the 11-10 audit: such RETESTs
// arrived hours late). A line's first candle after its anchor restarts (the session line's first
// of the day) can't fire: the "cross" there is the line starting over.
// Gainers only by default; `cross N` counts the day's crosses sent on the line, and the server
// announces the first few on Momentum names (TV_SETUP.em_cap), like the VB.
// v35 inputs go last.
emOn      = input.bool(true,     "EMA cross setup on (v35): an EMA crosses above a VWAP line, judged at a candle's close", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emTf      = input.timeframe("2", "EMA: candle timeframe (the EMA of its closes; judged at each close)", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emLen     = input.int(9,         "EMA: length", minval = 1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emSession = input.bool(true,     "EMA lines: session VWAP", inline = "eml", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emMonth   = input.bool(false,    "month VWAP", inline = "eml", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emYear    = input.bool(false,    "year VWAP", inline = "eml", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emGainOn  = input.bool(true,     "EMA: gainers only (the gainer filter at the top)", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emShow    = input.bool(true,     "EMA: draw the EMA line and the markers", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
// v36 inputs go last: the filter (operator, 11-13, PARA: "is there anyway we can filter/optimize the
// false ones?"). Measured on our data (research/ema-vwap, 08-14 → 11-13, 3,768 crosses): about half
// close back under the VWAP within 5 candles, and three things mark the worse ones in both halves of
// the data — the hour (before 07:00 ET: 60–64% false), a short stay under the line before the cross
// (under 5 candles: 56–62%) and crossing back and forth before it (5+ flips in 20 candles: 64%). The
// crosses this filter calls weak were false 57% of the time, the rest 41–44%; the plain cross loses
// either way (a heads-up, not an edge), and the ADX and volume filters of the video did nothing.
// A weak cross is drawn gray and its message says `| weak`: the server stores it and stays quiet.
emFilterOn = input.bool(true,    "EMA filter on (v36): weak crosses are drawn gray and sent quietly", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emMinUnder = input.int(5,        "EMA filter: the EMA was under the line for at least N candles before the cross", minval = 0, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emMaxFlips = input.int(2,        "EMA filter: at most N EMA / line crossings in the 20 candles before", minval = 0, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emFromHour = input.int(7,        "EMA filter: not before this hour, New York time (4 = from the pre-market open)", minval = 0, maxval = 23, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
// v37 inputs go last: the BOUNCE (operator, 11-13, PARA with v36's marks: "maybe, pullback or bounce
// from ema and/or vwap can help?"). Measured first (research/ema-vwap/ema_pullback_study.py, the same
// 3,768 crosses): waiting after a cross for a candle whose low comes down to the EMA or the VWAP and
// then a green close above the EMA takes about 44% of the crosses. Those entries close back under the
// VWAP within 5 candles 35% of the time (the cross itself: 48%) and lose about −0.08R with a stop
// under the pullback's low and a 2R target (the cross: −0.21R) — in both halves of the data, on 5m
// candles, and with a 5 or a 20 candle wait. The crosses that never give one are mostly the failures
// (65–70% false), not runs that got away. Fewer false ones and under half the loss; still not an edge.
// A bounce after a weak cross is weak too: gray, `| weak`, not announced.
emBncOn   = input.bool(true,           "EMA bounce on (v37): after an EMA cross, a pullback to the EMA or the VWAP, then a green close above the EMA", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncFrom = input.string("EMA or VWAP", "EMA bounce: the pullback comes down to", options = ["EMA or VWAP", "EMA", "VWAP"], group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncWait = input.int(10,              "EMA bounce: within N candles after the cross", minval = 1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncTolE = input.float(0.0,           "EMA bounce: a low within this % above the EMA counts as a touch", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncTolV = input.float(1.0,           "EMA bounce: a low within this % above the VWAP counts as a touch", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emBncE = emBncFrom != "VWAP"
emBncV = emBncFrom != "EMA"
// (v39's six MACD inputs, mcOn … mcShow, sat here until v44 removed the MACD cross after a DIP.)
// v40 input goes last: the line that crosses the VWAP (operator, 11-15: "can we make EMA Cross use
// BollingerBands upper row instead of EMA? So, add this to settings so I can switch between EMA and
// BB Upper row? We have a bb upper row already which we use for VWAP+BB Cross"; then: "or, could we
// do both?"). With "Both" each line runs on its own: its own crosses, day's numbers and alerts.
// v44: the default is "BB upper", the operator's live setting (it was "Both").
emSrc   = input.string("BB upper", "EMA cross: the line that crosses the VWAP (v40) — the EMA, the upper Bollinger Band (the VB's band: its BB timeframe, length and StdDev), or both, each with its own alerts", options = ["EMA", "BB upper", "Both"], group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
emUseE  = emSrc != "BB upper"   // the EMA's crosses (and its BOUNCE) are on
emUseB  = emSrc != "EMA"        // the band's crosses are on
// v41 input goes last (operator, 11-16, CLRO on a 1m chart: "bb upper row moves away from price if it
// drops too fast, and crosses up the near vwap"). A fast drop widens the band, and its upper line can
// rise over the VWAP while the price falls away from it. The test: the candle closed under the band's
// middle line (its 20-close average). A price that lifts the band closes above the middle; one that
// drops away closes under it. Such a cross is still sent, with `| weak`, and drawn gray.
// Measured (research/ema-vwap/band_cross_study.py, 08-14 → 11-14, a 1m band, 5,563 crosses on 3m
// candles): a quarter of the band's crosses are of this kind. On names already on our screen they
// were followed by a bounce more often than not (+0.2% to +0.8% five candles later, in both halves of
// the data) while the other three quarters lost on average (−0.5% to −0.6%) — so it marks a different
// event (a dip, not a push), not a worse one. The first push of a move from flat, the kind the
// operator showed (RBNE, GP), happens before a name reaches our screen and isn't in that data.
bbMidOn = input.bool(true, "BB cross (v41): a cross with the candle closing under the band's middle line (the band widened on a drop; the price didn't lift it) is drawn gray and sent quietly", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
// (v42's three BASIS inputs, bsOn / bsTf / bsLen, sat here until v44 removed the BASIS cross.)

// rsSym (the symbol with extended hours, for the request): the name comes from the RSI section, removed in v44.
rsSym = ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended)
// The EMA after the last finished candle of its timeframe, and live at this bar (that EMA's
// chart value now: the finished candles + this bar's close as the open one's).
emPrevE = request.security(rsSym, emTf, ta.ema(close, emLen)[1], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
emAlpha = 2.0 / (emLen + 1)
emLive  = emAlpha * close + (1 - emAlpha) * emPrevE
emTfSec = timeframe.in_seconds(emTf)

// v40: the upper Bollinger Band as a line that crosses the VWAP. It is the VB's band (the same BB
// timeframe, length and StdDev), built as vbStep builds it: the BB timeframe's last vbLen - 1
// finished closes plus the forming one, from the alert timeframe's bars (30s). So the alert and
// every chart read one line. A chart bigger than the alert timeframe replays those bars inside
// each of its bars and takes the band at the last one (the band at the chart bar's close).
// The band's crosses follow the EMA's rule and settings — judged at each close of the EMA's candle
// timeframe, above the VWAP line now and at or under it at the close before, the same lines,
// gainer filter and weak-cross filter — with their own state and day's numbers (section 4b,
// after the EMA's). They have no BOUNCE: that is a pullback to the EMA.
emBand(simple string bTf) =>
    bool bNew = timeframe.change(bTf)
    var bCloses = array.new<float>()
    var float bLastC = na
    if bNew and not na(bLastC)
        array.push(bCloses, bLastC)
        if array.size(bCloses) > vbLen - 1
            array.shift(bCloses)
    bLastC := close
    float bUp  = na
    float bMid = na          // v41: the band's middle line (the average the band is built around)
    int   bN   = array.size(bCloses)
    if bN == vbLen - 1
        float bSum = close
        for i = 0 to bN - 1
            bSum := bSum + array.get(bCloses, i)
        float bMean = bSum / vbLen
        float bSq   = math.pow(close - bMean, 2)
        for i = 0 to bN - 1
            bSq := bSq + math.pow(array.get(bCloses, i) - bMean, 2)
        bUp  := bMean + vbMult * math.sqrt(bSq / vbLen)
        bMid := bMean
    [bUp, bMid]
// rsChartSec (the chart's bar in seconds): the name comes from the RSI section, removed in v44.
rsChartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
// The band is the alert's on a chart of the alert timeframe or a multiple of it, with a band
// timeframe no smaller than it.
emBbOk    = rsChartSec >= vbBaseSec and rsChartSec % vbBaseSec == 0 and timeframe.in_seconds(vbBbTf) >= vbBaseSec
emBbLower = emOn and emUseB and emBbOk and rsChartSec > vbBaseSec and rsChartSec <= emTfSec and emTfSec % rsChartSec == 0
[emBbIn, emBbMidIn] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, emBbLower ? vbTf : timeframe.period, emBand(vbBbTf))
float emBb    = na
float emBbMid = na
if array.size(emBbIn) > 0
    emBb    := array.get(emBbIn, array.size(emBbIn) - 1)
    emBbMid := array.get(emBbMidIn, array.size(emBbMidIn) - 1)
// (v42's basis line, the middle of a separate band, was built here until v44 removed the BASIS cross.)
// Where the samples are right: a chart no bigger than the EMA's timeframe whose bars divide it.
// The EMA's crosses run there when the EMA is a chosen line; the band's (bbOk) where its line is
// right too.
emOk    = emOn and rsChartSec <= emTfSec and emTfSec % rsChartSec == 0 and emUseE
bbOk    = emOn and rsChartSec <= emTfSec and emTfSec % rsChartSec == 0 and emUseB and emBbOk

// One line's state, stepped once per sampled candle close.
type EmaLine
    float prevE = na    // the EMA and the line at the candle close before
    float prevL = na
    int   n     = 0     // the day's crosses sent on this line (v36: the weak ones aren't counted)
    int   under = 0     // v36: closes in a row with the EMA at or under the line, up to the last one
    int   ran   = 0     // v36: at the last cross, how many closes the EMA had been under the line…
    int   flips = 0     // …and how many times the two had crossed in the 20 closes before it
    bool  armed = false // v37: a cross is waiting for its bounce
    int   age   = 0     // candles since that cross's candle
    bool  hitE  = false // a candle's low has come down to the EMA since…
    bool  hitV  = false // …or to the line
    float lowP  = na    // the lowest low since that touch (the stop goes a tick under it)
    bool  weakX = false // the cross was weak (v36), so its bounce is
    int   bn    = 0     // the day's bounces sent on this line (the weak ones aren't counted)

// A candle close → true when the EMA crossed above the line. `hist` is this line's last 20 closes
// (1 = the EMA above the line), kept beside the object.
method crossUp(EmaLine s, array<int> hist, float e, float ln) =>
    bool up = not na(s.prevE) and not na(e) and not na(ln) and s.prevE <= s.prevL and e > ln
    if not na(e) and not na(ln)
        if up
            s.ran := s.under
            int f = 0
            int m = array.size(hist)
            if m > 1
                for i = 1 to m - 1
                    if array.get(hist, i) != array.get(hist, i - 1)
                        f += 1
            s.flips := f
        s.under := e > ln ? 0 : s.under + 1
        array.push(hist, e > ln ? 1 : 0)
        if array.size(hist) > 20
            array.shift(hist)
        s.prevE := e
        s.prevL := ln
    up

// The line's anchor restarted: its next candle has no close before it.
method restart(EmaLine s, array<int> hist) =>
    s.prevE := na
    s.prevL := na
    s.under := 0
    s.armed := false
    array.clear(hist)
    true

// v37: a sent cross starts the wait for its bounce (a newer cross starts it over).
method arm(EmaLine s, bool weak) =>
    s.armed := true
    s.age   := 0
    s.hitE  := false
    s.hitV  := false
    s.lowP  := na
    s.weakX := weak
    true

// v37: one candle close of the wait → true at the bounce. The candle's low comes down to the EMA or
// the line (a touch; from then on the lowest low is kept), and the same candle or a later one closes
// green above the EMA. A close under the line first, or emBncWait candles without one, ends the wait.
method stepBounce(EmaLine s, float e, float ln, float cOpen, float cLow, float cClose) =>
    bool go = false
    if s.armed and not na(e) and not na(ln) and not na(cOpen) and not na(cLow)
        s.age := s.age + 1
        if emBncE and cLow <= e * (1 + emBncTolE / 100)
            s.hitE := true
        if emBncV and cLow <= ln * (1 + emBncTolV / 100)
            s.hitV := true
        if s.hitE or s.hitV
            s.lowP := na(s.lowP) ? cLow : math.min(s.lowP, cLow)
        if cClose < ln
            s.armed := false
        else if (s.hitE or s.hitV) and cClose > cOpen and cClose > e
            go := true
            s.armed := false
        else if s.age >= emBncWait
            s.armed := false
    go

// v36: a weak cross — too early in the day, too short a stay under the line, or too much crossing before it.
emWeak(EmaLine s, bool early) => emFilterOn and (early or s.ran < emMinUnder or s.flips > emMaxFlips)

// The fired lines' best reading, for the message: the longest stay under the line and the fewest flips.
emRead(EmaLine s, EmaLine m, EmaLine y, bool fS, bool fM, bool fY) =>
    int u = 0
    int f = 999
    if fS
        u := math.max(u, s.ran)
        f := math.min(f, s.flips)
    if fM
        u := math.max(u, m.ran)
        f := math.min(f, m.flips)
    if fY
        u := math.max(u, y.ran)
        f := math.min(f, y.flips)
    [u, f]

// The lowest of the fired lines' counts (as the VB's `cross N`).
emCount(EmaLine s, EmaLine m, EmaLine y, bool fS, bool fM, bool fY) =>
    int n = 999
    if fS
        n := math.min(n, s.n)
    if fM
        n := math.min(n, m.n)
    if fY
        n := math.min(n, y.n)
    n

// v37: the fired lines' bounce, for the message — the lowest pullback low, the fewest candles since
// the cross, what the pullback came down to, and the lowest of the day's counts.
emBRead(EmaLine s, EmaLine m, EmaLine y, bool fS, bool fM, bool fY) =>
    float lo = na
    int   ag = 999
    bool  hE = false
    bool  hV = false
    int   n  = 999
    if fS
        lo := s.lowP
        ag := s.age
        hE := s.hitE
        hV := s.hitV
        n  := s.bn
    if fM
        lo := na(lo) ? m.lowP : math.min(lo, m.lowP)
        ag := math.min(ag, m.age)
        hE := hE or m.hitE
        hV := hV or m.hitV
        n  := math.min(n, m.bn)
    if fY
        lo := na(lo) ? y.lowP : math.min(lo, y.lowP)
        ag := math.min(ag, y.age)
        hE := hE or y.hitE
        hV := hV or y.hitV
        n  := math.min(n, y.bn)
    [lo, ag, hE, hV, n]

var EmaLine emS = EmaLine.new()
var EmaLine emM = EmaLine.new()
var EmaLine emY = EmaLine.new()
var emHS = array.new<int>()   // v36: each line's last 20 closes (1 = the EMA above it), for the flips
var emHM = array.new<int>()
var emHY = array.new<int>()
emT   = time(emTf)
emEnd = time_close == time_close(emTf)
var int emDone = na
bool emLateS = not na(emT[1]) and emT != emT[1] and (na(emDone) or emDone != emT[1])
bool emNewM  = timeframe.change("M")
bool emNewY  = timeframe.change("12M")
// v37: the open and the low of the EMA's candle so far, and of the one before (for a late sample).
var float emCO  = na
var float emCL  = na
var float emCOp = na
var float emCLp = na
if na(emT[1]) or emT != emT[1]
    emCOp := emCO
    emCLp := emCL
    emCO  := open
    emCL  := low
else
    emCL := math.min(emCL, low)
// A late sample's crosses (the candle before, from the bar before) and this bar's own; with each,
// the day's number, the stay under the line, the flips before, and whether the filter calls it weak.
bool emLS = false
bool emLM = false
bool emLY = false
int  emLN = 0
int  emLU = 0
int  emLF = 0
bool emLW = false
bool emCS = false
bool emCM = false
bool emCY = false
int  emCN = 0
int  emCU = 0
int  emCF = 0
bool emCW = false
// v37: the same for the bounces — the lines that fired, the day's number, the stop (a tick under the
// pullback's low), the candles since the cross, what the pullback came down to, and weak or not.
bool  emBLS = false
bool  emBLM = false
bool  emBLY = false
int   emBLN = 0
float emBLStop = na
int   emBLAge = 0
bool  emBLE = false
bool  emBLV = false
bool  emBLW = false
bool  emBCS = false
bool  emBCM = false
bool  emBCY = false
int   emBCN = 0
float emBCStop = na
int   emBCAge = 0
bool  emBCE = false
bool  emBCV = false
bool  emBCW = false
if emOk
    if emLateS
        bool emOkL = inWindow and not newDay and (not emGainOn or gainer[1])
        // v37: an earlier cross's bounce first (a cross candle can't be its own bounce). Weak when none
        // of its lines' crosses was strong; only a strong bounce takes a day's number.
        bool emB1 = emBncOn and emSession and emS.stepBounce(emLive[1], svwap[1], emCOp, emCLp, close[1])
        bool emB2 = emBncOn and emMonth and emM.stepBounce(emLive[1], mvwap[1], emCOp, emCLp, close[1])
        bool emB3 = emBncOn and emYear and emY.stepBounce(emLive[1], yvwap[1], emCOp, emCLp, close[1])
        emBLS := emB1 and emOkL
        emBLM := emB2 and emOkL
        emBLY := emB3 and emOkL
        bool emH1 = emBLS and not emS.weakX
        bool emH2 = emBLM and not emM.weakX
        bool emH3 = emBLY and not emY.weakX
        emBLW := not (emH1 or emH2 or emH3)
        if emH1
            emS.bn := emS.bn + 1
        if emH2
            emM.bn := emM.bn + 1
        if emH3
            emY.bn := emY.bn + 1
        bool emQ1 = emBLW ? emBLS : emH1
        bool emQ2 = emBLW ? emBLM : emH2
        bool emQ3 = emBLW ? emBLY : emH3
        [emBLo1, emBAg1, emBE1, emBV1, emBN1] = emBRead(emS, emM, emY, emQ1, emQ2, emQ3)
        emBLStop := emBLo1 - syminfo.mintick
        emBLAge  := emBAg1
        emBLE    := emBE1
        emBLV    := emBV1
        emBLN    := emBN1
        bool emX1 = emSession and emS.crossUp(emHS, emLive[1], svwap[1])
        bool emX2 = emMonth and emM.crossUp(emHM, emLive[1], mvwap[1])
        bool emX3 = emYear and emY.crossUp(emHY, emLive[1], yvwap[1])
        emDone := emT[1]
        emLS := emX1 and emOkL
        emLM := emX2 and emOkL
        emLY := emX3 and emOkL
        // v36: the strong ones among them (the hour is the candle's own, by its open). Only a strong
        // cross takes a day's number, and a message is weak when none of its lines is strong.
        bool emEarlyL = hour(emT[1], "America/New_York") < emFromHour
        bool emG1 = emLS and not emWeak(emS, emEarlyL)
        bool emG2 = emLM and not emWeak(emM, emEarlyL)
        bool emG3 = emLY and not emWeak(emY, emEarlyL)
        emLW := not (emG1 or emG2 or emG3)
        if emG1
            emS.n := emS.n + 1
        if emG2
            emM.n := emM.n + 1
        if emG3
            emY.n := emY.n + 1
        // The message's numbers: the strong lines' when there is one, else the fired lines' (a weak
        // cross then carries the day's count so far, 0 before the first strong one).
        bool emP1 = emLW ? emLS : emG1
        bool emP2 = emLW ? emLM : emG2
        bool emP3 = emLW ? emLY : emG3
        emLN := emCount(emS, emM, emY, emP1, emP2, emP3)
        [emU1, emF1] = emRead(emS, emM, emY, emP1, emP2, emP3)
        emLU := emU1
        emLF := emF1
        // v37: a sent cross starts the wait for its bounce (weak if the cross was).
        if emLS
            emS.arm(not emG1)
        if emLM
            emM.arm(not emG2)
        if emLY
            emY.arm(not emG3)
    // The anchors: a new day restarts the session line and the day's counts, and ends every wait.
    if newDay
        emS.restart(emHS)
        emS.n := 0
        emM.n := 0
        emY.n := 0
        emS.bn := 0
        emM.bn := 0
        emY.bn := 0
        emM.armed := false
        emY.armed := false
    if emNewM
        emM.restart(emHM)
    if emNewY
        emY.restart(emHY)
    if emEnd and (na(emDone) or emDone != emT)
        bool emOkC = inWindow and (not emGainOn or gainer)
        bool emB4 = emBncOn and emSession and emS.stepBounce(emLive, svwap, emCO, emCL, close)
        bool emB5 = emBncOn and emMonth and emM.stepBounce(emLive, mvwap, emCO, emCL, close)
        bool emB6 = emBncOn and emYear and emY.stepBounce(emLive, yvwap, emCO, emCL, close)
        emBCS := emB4 and emOkC
        emBCM := emB5 and emOkC
        emBCY := emB6 and emOkC
        bool emH4 = emBCS and not emS.weakX
        bool emH5 = emBCM and not emM.weakX
        bool emH6 = emBCY and not emY.weakX
        emBCW := not (emH4 or emH5 or emH6)
        if emH4
            emS.bn := emS.bn + 1
        if emH5
            emM.bn := emM.bn + 1
        if emH6
            emY.bn := emY.bn + 1
        bool emQ4 = emBCW ? emBCS : emH4
        bool emQ5 = emBCW ? emBCM : emH5
        bool emQ6 = emBCW ? emBCY : emH6
        [emBLo2, emBAg2, emBE2, emBV2, emBN2] = emBRead(emS, emM, emY, emQ4, emQ5, emQ6)
        emBCStop := emBLo2 - syminfo.mintick
        emBCAge  := emBAg2
        emBCE    := emBE2
        emBCV    := emBV2
        emBCN    := emBN2
        bool emX4 = emSession and emS.crossUp(emHS, emLive, svwap)
        bool emX5 = emMonth and emM.crossUp(emHM, emLive, mvwap)
        bool emX6 = emYear and emY.crossUp(emHY, emLive, yvwap)
        emDone := emT
        emCS := emX4 and emOkC
        emCM := emX5 and emOkC
        emCY := emX6 and emOkC
        bool emEarlyC = hour(emT, "America/New_York") < emFromHour
        bool emG4 = emCS and not emWeak(emS, emEarlyC)
        bool emG5 = emCM and not emWeak(emM, emEarlyC)
        bool emG6 = emCY and not emWeak(emY, emEarlyC)
        emCW := not (emG4 or emG5 or emG6)
        if emG4
            emS.n := emS.n + 1
        if emG5
            emM.n := emM.n + 1
        if emG6
            emY.n := emY.n + 1
        bool emP4 = emCW ? emCS : emG4
        bool emP5 = emCW ? emCM : emG5
        bool emP6 = emCW ? emCY : emG6
        emCN := emCount(emS, emM, emY, emP4, emP5, emP6)
        [emU2, emF2] = emRead(emS, emM, emY, emP4, emP5, emP6)
        emCU := emU2
        emCF := emF2
        if emCS
            emS.arm(not emG4)
        if emCM
            emM.arm(not emG5)
        if emCY
            emY.arm(not emG6)

// ── 4b) THE BAND'S CROSSES (v40) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
// The upper Bollinger Band (emBb, above) against the same VWAP lines, by the EMA's rule and with the
// EMA's settings: sampled at each close of the EMA's candle timeframe (a candle whose closing bar had
// no trades on the next bar, never across the day's end), above the line now and at or under it at
// the close before, the day's first candle excluded, gainers only, the v36 filter's three tests on
// the band's own stay under the line and crossings. Its own lines, so its own `cross N` per day.
// One sample of the three lines → the lines that fired, the day's number, the stay under the line,
// the flips before, and whether the filter calls it weak (as the EMA's block above does inline).
// v41: `px` and `mid` are the sampled candle's close and the band's middle line then; with bbMidOn a
// close under the middle makes the cross weak, whatever the v36 filter says.
bbSample(EmaLine s, EmaLine m, EmaLine y, array<int> hs, array<int> hm, array<int> hy, float b, float sv, float mv, float yv, bool ok, bool early, float px, float mid) =>
    bool x1 = emSession and s.crossUp(hs, b, sv)
    bool x2 = emMonth and m.crossUp(hm, b, mv)
    bool x3 = emYear and y.crossUp(hy, b, yv)
    bool f1 = x1 and ok
    bool f2 = x2 and ok
    bool f3 = x3 and ok
    bool drop = bbMidOn and not na(mid) and px < mid
    bool g1 = f1 and not drop and not emWeak(s, early)
    bool g2 = f2 and not drop and not emWeak(m, early)
    bool g3 = f3 and not drop and not emWeak(y, early)
    bool weak = not (g1 or g2 or g3)
    if g1
        s.n := s.n + 1
    if g2
        m.n := m.n + 1
    if g3
        y.n := y.n + 1
    bool p1 = weak ? f1 : g1
    bool p2 = weak ? f2 : g2
    bool p3 = weak ? f3 : g3
    int n = emCount(s, m, y, p1, p2, p3)
    [u, f] = emRead(s, m, y, p1, p2, p3)
    [f1, f2, f3, n, u, f, weak]

var EmaLine bbS = EmaLine.new()
var EmaLine bbM = EmaLine.new()
var EmaLine bbY = EmaLine.new()
var bbHS = array.new<int>()
var bbHM = array.new<int>()
var bbHY = array.new<int>()
var int bbDone = na
bool bbLateS = not na(emT[1]) and emT != emT[1] and (na(bbDone) or bbDone != emT[1])
bool bbLS = false
bool bbLM = false
bool bbLY = false
int  bbLN = 0
int  bbLU = 0
int  bbLF = 0
bool bbLW = false
bool bbCS = false
bool bbCM = false
bool bbCY = false
int  bbCN = 0
int  bbCU = 0
int  bbCF = 0
bool bbCW = false
if bbOk
    if bbLateS
        bool bbOkL    = inWindow and not newDay and (not emGainOn or gainer[1])
        bool bbEarlyL = hour(emT[1], "America/New_York") < emFromHour
        [bbA1, bbA2, bbA3, bbA4, bbA5, bbA6, bbA7] = bbSample(bbS, bbM, bbY, bbHS, bbHM, bbHY, emBb[1], svwap[1], mvwap[1], yvwap[1], bbOkL, bbEarlyL, close[1], emBbMid[1])
        bbDone := emT[1]
        bbLS := bbA1
        bbLM := bbA2
        bbLY := bbA3
        bbLN := bbA4
        bbLU := bbA5
        bbLF := bbA6
        bbLW := bbA7
    // The anchors: a new day restarts the session line and the day's counts.
    if newDay
        bbS.restart(bbHS)
        bbS.n := 0
        bbM.n := 0
        bbY.n := 0
    if emNewM
        bbM.restart(bbHM)
    if emNewY
        bbY.restart(bbHY)
    if emEnd and (na(bbDone) or bbDone != emT)
        bool bbOkC    = inWindow and (not emGainOn or gainer)
        bool bbEarlyC = hour(emT, "America/New_York") < emFromHour
        [bbB1, bbB2, bbB3, bbB4, bbB5, bbB6, bbB7] = bbSample(bbS, bbM, bbY, bbHS, bbHM, bbHY, emBb, svwap, mvwap, yvwap, bbOkC, bbEarlyC, close, emBbMid)
        bbDone := emT
        bbCS := bbB1
        bbCM := bbB2
        bbCY := bbB3
        bbCN := bbB4
        bbCU := bbB5
        bbCF := bbB6
        bbCW := bbB7

// (v42's section 4c, the basis's crosses, sat here until v44 removed the BASIS cross.)

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage. Every value is the sampled
// candle's (a late one's from the bar before):
//   EMA OMH 8.09 | sVWAP 8.01 (+1.0%) | mVWAP 7.5 (+7.9%) | ema 9 8.03 | line session | candle 3 | cross 1 | under 12 | flips 1 | day high +25% | vwap 30s | tf 30S
// v40, a cross of the band (`band` = true; `e` is then the band): `| upper 8.03 (+0.7%) | bb 45S` —
// the band, the price against it and its timeframe, as in a CROSS — in the place of `| ema 9 8.03`:
//   EMA OMH 8.09 | sVWAP 8.01 (+1.0%) | upper 8.03 (+0.7%) | bb 45S | line session | candle 3 | cross 1 | under 12 | flips 1 | day high +25% | vwap 30s | tf 30S
// v36: `under N` = the candles the EMA had been at or under the line, `flips N` = its crossings of the
// line in the 20 candles before, and `| weak` after them when the filter calls the cross weak.
emPct(float px, float ln) => (px >= ln ? "+" : "") + str.tostring((px / ln - 1) * 100, "#.0")
// v41: a band cross also carries `| mid 8.05 (+0.5%)` after `bb` — the band's middle line and the
// price against it (under it = the band widened on a drop).
// `kind` names the line that crossed: "ema" or "bb" (the band); v42's third kind, the basis, went
// with the BASIS cross in v44. (Not `by`: that is a reserved word in Pine, and v42's first paste
// failed to compile on it.)
emMsgBy(bool fS, bool fM, bool fY, int n, float px, float e, float sv, float mv, float yv, bool late, int under, int flips, bool weak, string kind, float mid) =>
    string names = ""
    if fS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
    if fM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
    if fY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
    string msg = "EMA " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(px, format.mintick)
    if not na(sv)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(sv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, sv) + "%)"
    if not na(mv)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, mv) + "%)"
    if not na(yv)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, yv) + "%)"
    if kind == "bb"
        msg += " | upper " + str.tostring(e, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, e) + "%) | bb " + vbBbTf
        if not na(mid)
            msg += " | mid " + str.tostring(mid, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, mid) + "%)"
    else
        msg += " | ema " + str.tostring(emLen) + " " + str.tostring(e, format.mintick)
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + emTf + " | cross " + str.tostring(n)
    msg += " | under " + str.tostring(under) + " | flips " + str.tostring(flips)
    if weak
        msg += " | weak"
    if not na(dayHighGain)
        msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if late
        msg += " | late"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period
// The EMA's and the band's messages, as their alerts have called them since v40 / v41.
emMsg(bool fS, bool fM, bool fY, int n, float px, float e, float sv, float mv, float yv, bool late, int under, int flips, bool weak, bool band, float mid) =>
    emMsgBy(fS, fM, fY, n, px, e, sv, mv, yv, late, under, flips, weak, band ? "bb" : "ema", mid)

// v37, the bounce's message (the same contract):
//   BOUNCE PARA 0.1021 | stop 0.0985 | sVWAP 0.0975 (+4.7%) | ema 9 0.099 | line session | from ema+vwap | candle 3 | bounce 1 | since 3 | day high +25% | vwap 30s | tf 30S
// `stop` = a tick under the pullback's low, `from` = what the pullback came down to (ema, vwap or
// ema+vwap), `since N` = candles after the cross candle, `| weak` when its cross was weak.
emBncMsg(bool fS, bool fM, bool fY, int n, float px, float e, float sv, float mv, float yv, bool late, float stop, int age, bool hitE, bool hitV, bool weak) =>
    string names = ""
    if fS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
    if fM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
    if fY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
    string msg = "BOUNCE " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(px, format.mintick) + " | stop " + str.tostring(stop, format.mintick)
    if not na(sv)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(sv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, sv) + "%)"
    if not na(mv)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, mv) + "%)"
    if not na(yv)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yv, format.mintick) + " (" + emPct(px, yv) + "%)"
    msg += " | ema " + str.tostring(emLen) + " " + str.tostring(e, format.mintick)
    msg += " | line " + names + " | from " + (hitE and hitV ? "ema+vwap" : hitE ? "ema" : "vwap")
    msg += " | candle " + emTf + " | bounce " + str.tostring(n) + " | since " + str.tostring(age)
    if weak
        msg += " | weak"
    if not na(dayHighGain)
        msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if late
        msg += " | late"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period

// From the 30s alert alone (the VB's alert timeframe), like the VB.
if (emBLS or emBLM or emBLY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emBncMsg(emBLS, emBLM, emBLY, emBLN, close[1], emLive[1], svwap[1], mvwap[1], yvwap[1], true, emBLStop, emBLAge, emBLE, emBLV, emBLW), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if (emBCS or emBCM or emBCY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emBncMsg(emBCS, emBCM, emBCY, emBCN, close, emLive, svwap, mvwap, yvwap, false, emBCStop, emBCAge, emBCE, emBCV, emBCW), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if (emLS or emLM or emLY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emMsg(emLS, emLM, emLY, emLN, close[1], emLive[1], svwap[1], mvwap[1], yvwap[1], true, emLU, emLF, emLW, false, na), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if (emCS or emCM or emCY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emMsg(emCS, emCM, emCY, emCN, close, emLive, svwap, mvwap, yvwap, false, emCU, emCF, emCW, false, na), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
// v40: the band's crosses, the same message with the band in the EMA's place (v41: and its middle line).
if (bbLS or bbLM or bbLY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emMsg(bbLS, bbLM, bbLY, bbLN, close[1], emBb[1], svwap[1], mvwap[1], yvwap[1], true, bbLU, bbLF, bbLW, true, emBbMid[1]), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if (bbCS or bbCM or bbCY) and timeframe.period == vbTf
    alert(emMsg(bbCS, bbCM, bbCY, bbCN, close, emBb, svwap, mvwap, yvwap, false, bbCU, bbCF, bbCW, true, emBbMid), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
// (v42's two BASIS alerts sat here until v44 removed the BASIS cross.)
// v35 plots go last: the EMA line, the markers, and a VWAP line this setup uses that no other draws.
plot(emOk and emShow ? emLive : na, "EMA (EMA cross, v35)", color.aqua)
plotshape(emShow and (emCS or emCM or emCY) and not emCW, "EMA cross (v35)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.orange, text = "EMA", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(emShow and (emLS or emLM or emLY) and not emLW, "EMA cross, late close (v35)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.orange, text = "EMA", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small, offset = -1)
plot(emOn and emSession and not ((pbOn and pbSession) or (vbOn and vbSession)) ? svwap : na, "sVWAP (EMA cross, v35)", color.purple)
plot(emOn and emMonth and not ((pbOn and pbMonth) or (vbOn and vbMonth)) ? mvwap : na, "mVWAP (EMA cross, v35)", color.yellow)
plot(emOn and emYear and not ((pbOn and pbYear) or (vbOn and vbYear)) ? yvwap : na, "yVWAP (EMA cross, v35)", color.blue)
// v36 plots go last: the crosses the filter calls weak, in gray (sent with `| weak`, stored, not announced).
plotshape(emShow and (emCS or emCM or emCY) and emCW, "EMA cross, filtered (v36)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "ema", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(emShow and (emLS or emLM or emLY) and emLW, "EMA cross, filtered, late close (v36)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "ema", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, offset = -1)
// v37 plots go last: the bounce after a cross (green), and the ones after a weak cross (gray).
plotshape(emShow and (emBCS or emBCM or emBCY) and not emBCW, "EMA bounce (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "BNC", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(emShow and (emBLS or emBLM or emBLY) and not emBLW, "EMA bounce, late close (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "BNC", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small, offset = -1)
plotshape(emShow and (emBCS or emBCM or emBCY) and emBCW, "EMA bounce, filtered (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "bnc", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(emShow and (emBLS or emBLM or emBLY) and emBLW, "EMA bounce, filtered, late close (v37)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "bnc", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, offset = -1)

// (v39's MACD cross after a DIP, section 5, sat here until v44 removed it.)
// v40 plots go last: the band where its crosses run and the VB isn't already drawing it on this
// chart, and the band's crosses (maroon "BB"; gray "bb" for the ones the filter calls weak).
plot(bbOk and emShow and not (vbShow and (vbLower or (vbOk and vbChartSec == vbBaseSec))) ? emBb : na, "BB upper (EMA cross, v40)", color.new(color.orange, 20))
plotshape(emShow and (bbCS or bbCM or bbCY) and not bbCW, "BB upper cross over VWAP (v40)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.maroon, text = "BB", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(emShow and (bbLS or bbLM or bbLY) and not bbLW, "BB upper cross, late close (v40)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.maroon, text = "BB", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small, offset = -1)
plotshape(emShow and (bbCS or bbCM or bbCY) and bbCW, "BB upper cross, filtered (v40)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "bb", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(emShow and (bbLS or bbLM or bbLY) and bbLW, "BB upper cross, filtered, late close (v40)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "bb", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny, offset = -1)
// v41 plot goes last: the band's middle line, hidden until switched on in Style (a cross whose candle
// closed under it is the gray kind).
plot(bbOk and emShow ? emBbMid : na, "BB middle (EMA cross, v41)", color.new(color.orange, 60), display = display.none)
// (v42's five BASIS plots sat here until v44 removed the BASIS cross.)

// ── 6) THE PULLBACK'S BASIS LINE (v45) ────────────────────────────────────────
// Operator, 11-22, with TradingView's own "BB 15S 20 SMA close" on a 1m chart, only its middle
// line shown: "add own BollingerBand to Pullback section, with configurable timeframe, only basis
// row is enough … I'm going to experiment entering when price closes above it after the pullback".
// The basis (middle line) of a Bollinger Band is the SMA of the closes; the band's StdDev doesn't
// move it, so there is no StdDev input. A line only: no alert, no marker, nothing sent, so the
// alerts need not be recreated for it. Drawn while the Pullback setup is on.
// It is the SMA on the band's own timeframe, read at each chart bar's close, which is what
// TradingView's built-in draws when its timeframe is set under the chart's. On bigger bars (15S
// on a 1m chart) it comes from a lower-timeframe request: the value at the last 15s bar inside
// the chart bar (a chart bar with none keeps the line where it was). On bars of the same size
// it is the chart's own SMA. On smaller bars (a 1m basis on a 30s chart) it comes from a plain
// request. Its three inputs are the script's last and show in the "Pullback to VWAP" group; its
// requests come after the hourly anchors (they need 20 bars, not a long history, see the note
// at anchorsBefore()); its plot is the script's last.
pbBsOn  = input.bool(true,       "Pullback basis line (v45): the basis (middle line) of a Bollinger Band of its own timeframe — a line to time an entry after a pullback, no alert", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbBsTf  = input.timeframe("15S", "Pullback basis: its band's timeframe", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbBsLen = input.int(20,          "Pullback basis: its band's length (the closes it averages)", minval = 1, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbBsSec   = timeframe.in_seconds(pbBsTf)
pbBsLower = pbOn and pbBsOn and pbBsSec < chartSec
pbBsUpper = pbOn and pbBsOn and pbBsSec > chartSec
pbBsIn    = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, pbBsLower ? pbBsTf : timeframe.period, ta.sma(close, pbBsLen))
pbBsHtf   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, pbBsUpper ? pbBsTf : timeframe.period, ta.sma(close, pbBsLen))
var float pbBasis = na
if pbBsUpper
    pbBasis := pbBsHtf
else if array.size(pbBsIn) > 0
    pbBasis := array.get(pbBsIn, array.size(pbBsIn) - 1)
plot(pbOn and pbBsOn ? pbBasis : na, "Pullback basis (v45)", color.white)

// ── 7) THE BAND CROSS'S BASIS LINE (v46) ──────────────────────────────────────
// Operator, 11-24: "add own BollingerBands basis row to the BB setups, as we did for Pullback";
// then, with the "EMA cross over VWAP" settings open (the line set to "BB upper"): "I mean, bb
// basis for this bb setups of EMA Cross Over VWAP".
// One more line, built like the pullback's (section 6): the basis (middle line) of a Bollinger
// Band of its own timeframe and length, which is the SMA of that timeframe's closes, read at each
// chart bar's close. It belongs to the EMA cross setup, whose line the operator runs as the band
// ("BB upper"), and is drawn while that setup is on. A line only: no alert, no marker, nothing
// sent, so the alerts need not be recreated for it. It is not the band cross's own band (the
// VB's, whose middle line the v41 test reads): it has its own switch, timeframe and length, so
// it can differ from that band and from the pullback's line; with the pullback's timeframe and
// length the two lines sit on top of each other.
// Its three inputs are the script's last and show in the "EMA cross over VWAP" group; its two
// requests and its plot are the script's last.
bbBsOn  = input.bool(true,       "Band cross basis line (v46): the basis (middle line) of a Bollinger Band of its own timeframe — a line to time an entry after a band cross, no alert", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
bbBsTf  = input.timeframe("15S", "Band cross basis: its band's timeframe", group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
bbBsLen = input.int(20,          "Band cross basis: its band's length (the closes it averages)", minval = 1, group = "EMA cross over VWAP (v35)")
bbBsUse   = emOn and bbBsOn
bbBsSec   = timeframe.in_seconds(bbBsTf)
bbBsLower = bbBsUse and bbBsSec < chartSec
bbBsUpper = bbBsUse and bbBsSec > chartSec
bbBsIn    = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, bbBsLower ? bbBsTf : timeframe.period, ta.sma(close, bbBsLen))
bbBsHtf   = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, bbBsUpper ? bbBsTf : timeframe.period, ta.sma(close, bbBsLen))
var float bbBasis = na
if bbBsUpper
    bbBasis := bbBsHtf
else if array.size(bbBsIn) > 0
    bbBasis := array.get(bbBsIn, array.size(bbBsIn) - 1)
plot(bbBsUse ? bbBasis : na, "Band cross basis (v46)", color.teal)

// ── 8) TURN: THE BOUNCE OFF A BASIS THAT HAS TURNED UP (v47) ──────────────────
// Operator, 11-25, with section 7's line at 1 minute / 15 closes and a MACD 12 26 9 under a 1m
// chart, on three moves of NIVF and one of APUS: "How can I catch such moves? … candle breaks the
// bb basis, the bb basis moving up, macd turned green, and price pulls back to bb basis line and
// bounces and this bounce is a signal"; "The most important part is, bb basis goes down (usually
// big drop), and after that, it starts moving up, price crosses it, and bounces (also, macd turns
// green)". Then: "I want to experiment with it, let's build it … a separate setup … with its own
// bb basis settings (macd usually standart)".
// The rule, on the candles of the basis's own timeframe (the chart must be on it):
//   break    a close above the basis after a close at or under it
//   touch    on a later candle, within N, the low comes down to the basis (at or under it, or
//            within the tolerance above it)
//   bounce   that candle or a later one (still within N) closes green and above the basis, with
//            the basis rising and (a switch) the MACD above its signal line. A close under the
//            basis first ends the wait. One bounce per break.
//   TURN     a bounce after the basis fell: its lowest value in the 31 candles to the bounce is no
//            older than `tnLowBars` candles and at least `tnFallMin` % under its highest value in
//            the 46 candles up to that low. A bounce without that fall uses up its break and
//            sends nothing.
// Measured before building (research/ema-vwap/basis_bounce_study.py, 71 days of our 1m bars): the
// fall is the condition that counts (+5% before a close back under the basis for 3–5% of bounces
// after no fall, 19–21% after a fall of 10% or more, about 20 a day on Momentum names); the MACD
// and the rising basis add nothing measurable; about break-even with a stop under the pullback's
// low. An experiment, as the operator asked.
// It reads the chart's own candles, so it runs where the chart's timeframe is the basis's: its
// markers on that chart, its alert from the alert on that timeframe (1m by default). No request.
// Message (the contract with parseTvMessage):
//   TURN NIVF 0.0213 | stop 0.0206 | sVWAP 0.0211 (+0.9%) | mVWAP 0.023 (-7.4%) | sma 15 0.0207 (+2.9%) | fall 12.3% | candle 1 | turn 1 | since 3 | green 1 | day high +25% | vwap 30s | tf 1
// `stop` = a tick under the pullback's lowest low, `sma N` = the basis and the price against it,
// `fall` = how far the basis fell before its low, `turn N` = the day's TURNs on this ticker,
// `since N` = candles after the break, `green` = the MACD above its signal at the bounce (1 / 0).
// Its thirteen inputs are the script's last; its two plots are the script's last.
tnOn      = input.bool(true,      "TURN setup on (v47): after its basis fell and turned up, price closes above the basis, comes back to it and bounces", group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnTf      = input.timeframe("1",  "TURN: the basis's timeframe — its candles are the ones judged; the markers show on that chart, the alert comes from the alert on it", group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnLen     = input.int(15,         "TURN: the basis's length (the closes it averages)", minval = 2, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnFallMin = input.float(10.0,     "TURN: the basis fell at least this % before its low (0 = no fall needed)", minval = 0, step = 0.5, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnLowBars = input.int(15,         "TURN: …and that low is within the last N candles", minval = 1, maxval = 30, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnTol     = input.float(1.0,      "TURN: a low within this % above the basis counts as the pullback reaching it", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnWaitN   = input.int(10,         "TURN: the bounce comes within N candles after the close above the basis", minval = 1, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnMacdOn  = input.bool(true,      "TURN: the MACD must be green at the bounce (above its signal line)", group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnFast    = input.int(12,         "TURN: the MACD's fast length", minval = 1, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnSlow    = input.int(26,         "TURN: the MACD's slow length", minval = 2, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnSig     = input.int(9,          "TURN: the MACD's signal length", minval = 1, group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnGainOn  = input.bool(true,      "TURN: gainers only (the gainer filter at the top)", group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnShow    = input.bool(true,      "TURN: draw its basis line and the markers", group = "TURN: the bounce off a basis that turned up (v47)")
tnRun     = tnOn and timeframe.in_seconds(tnTf) == chartSec
tnB       = ta.sma(close, tnLen)
[tnMacdLine, tnSignalLine, tnHist] = ta.macd(close, tnFast, tnSlow, tnSig)
tnGreen   = tnHist > 0
// The fall: the basis's lowest value in the 31 candles to this one, how many candles ago it was,
// and its highest value in the 46 candles up to that low.
tnLowAgo  = -ta.lowestbars(tnB, 31)
tnLowVal  = ta.lowest(tnB, 31)
tnHigh46  = ta.highest(tnB, 46)
tnPeak    = tnHigh46[tnLowAgo]
tnFallPct = not na(tnPeak) and tnPeak > 0 ? (1 - tnLowVal / tnPeak) * 100 : na
tnFell    = tnFallMin <= 0 or (not na(tnFallPct) and tnLowAgo <= tnLowBars and tnFallPct >= tnFallMin)
var bool  tnWaiting  = false   // a break is open: waiting for the touch and the bounce
var int   tnBreakBar = na
var float tnPbLow    = na      // the pullback's lowest low (it starts at the break candle's close)
var bool  tnTouched  = false
var int   tnCount    = 0       // the day's TURNs on this ticker
if newDay
    tnCount   := 0
    tnWaiting := false
bool  tnFire = false
float tnStop = na
int   tnAge  = na
if tnRun and not na(tnB) and not na(tnB[1])
    bool tnRising = tnB > tnB[1]
    if tnWaiting
        if close < tnB
            tnWaiting := false
        else
            tnPbLow := math.min(tnPbLow, low)
            if low <= tnB * (1 + tnTol / 100)
                tnTouched := true
            if tnTouched and close > open and close > tnB and tnRising and (not tnMacdOn or tnGreen)
                // the bounce: it uses up the break, whether or not the fall and the filters let it send
                tnWaiting := false
                if tnFell and inWindow and (not tnGainOn or gainer)
                    tnFire  := true
                    tnStop  := tnPbLow - syminfo.mintick
                    tnAge   := bar_index - tnBreakBar
                    tnCount += 1
            else if bar_index - tnBreakBar >= tnWaitN
                tnWaiting := false
    if not tnWaiting and not tnFire and close > tnB and close[1] <= tnB[1]
        tnWaiting  := true
        tnBreakBar := bar_index
        tnPbLow    := close
        tnTouched  := false
tnMsg() =>
    string msg = "TURN " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick) + " | stop " + str.tostring(tnStop, format.mintick)
    if not na(svwap)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(svwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(svwap) + "%)"
    if not na(mvwap)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(mvwap) + "%)"
    if not na(yvwap)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(yvwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | sma " + str.tostring(tnLen) + " " + str.tostring(tnB, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(tnB) + "%)"
    if not na(tnFallPct)
        msg += " | fall " + str.tostring(tnFallPct, "#.0") + "%"
    msg += " | candle " + tnTf + " | turn " + str.tostring(tnCount) + " | since " + str.tostring(tnAge) + " | green " + (tnGreen ? "1" : "0")
    if not na(dayHighGain)
        msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period
if tnFire
    alert(tnMsg(), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plot(tnRun and tnShow ? tnB : na, "TURN basis (v47)", color.fuchsia)
plotshape(tnShow and tnFire, "TURN (v47)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.fuchsia, text = "TN", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)

// ── 9) POP AND BACK: A POP OFF THE BASIS AND ITS FIRST PULLBACK (v48) ─────────
// Operator, 11-26, with a basis line at 1 minute / 15 closes on 1m charts of SVRE, ZNB, APUS and
// WHLR: "these moves are initial pop, and their first pullback to bb basis row … how to catch such
// pullbacks?"; then: "I'm thinking how to catch them up, while the initial pop is moveing too
// fast". Buying the pop's own candle was measured first and loses (research/ema-vwap/pop_study.py:
// a third of the pops are back under the basis within 5 candles), so the setup has two steps, like
// CROSS and RETEST, and the operator said "yes, lets do that":
//   POP    a heads-up, no entry: open the chart and be ready
//   BACK   the entry: the first pullback to the basis after the POP, at its bounce
// The rule, on the candles of the basis's own timeframe (the chart must be on it):
//   run      starts at a close above the basis after a close at or under it (or at the day's
//            first candle, if it closes above the basis) and ends at a close under the basis,
//            or with the day: a run never carries over into the next day
//   POP      the first candle of a run by which a high of the run has reached `ppUp` % above the
//            basis. One POP per run.
//   touch    on a candle after the POP candle, the low comes down to the basis (at or under it, or
//            within the tolerance above it)
//   BACK     that candle or a later one closes green and above the basis, with the basis rising
//            and (a switch) the MACD above its signal line, within `ppWaitN` candles of the POP
//            candle. The run's end (a close under the basis) ends the wait. One BACK per POP.
//            The touch is remembered until the bounce: where the MACD turns green a few candles
//            after the low, the BACK comes at that later close, above the basis (the message's
//            `sma N … (+x%)` says how far; measured, a BACK 5% or more above the basis has the
//            far stop and is the worse kind)
//   stop     a tick under the lowest low after the candle of the run's highest high as it stood
//            before the bounce candle, the bounce candle's own low included (so a bounce candle
//            that makes the new high itself keeps the pullback's low)
// The gainer filter and the alert window are read at each alert's own candle, so a BACK can be
// sent after a POP that was not (the ticker became a gainer in between), and the other way round.
// Measured on the built rule (research/ema-vwap/pop_back_study.py, 71 days of our 1m bars, both
// halves): at 10% about 35 POPs a day on Momentum names (28 after the dashboard's 3 a day per
// ticker); a BACK follows 28% of them, a median 7 candles later and 1–2% under the POP candle's
// close; about 10 BACKs a day; +5% before a close back under the basis for 29–35% of them, +10%
// for 16–20%; −0.05R to −0.08R with the stop and a 2R target, so about break-even. At 5% there are
// 110–130 POPs a day and the BACKs do worse (−0.22R). An experiment, as the operator asked.
// A TURN (section 8) and a BACK can fire on one candle (a fall, then a pop, then the bounce): they
// are separate setups and both are sent.
// It reads the chart's own candles, so it runs where the chart's timeframe is the basis's: its
// markers on that chart, its alerts from the alert on that timeframe (1m by default). No request.
// Messages (the contract with parseTvMessage):
//   POP SVRE 1.85 | sVWAP 1.62 (+14.2%) | mVWAP 1.4 (+32.1%) | sma 15 1.66 (+11.4%) | ran 12.6% | candle 1 | pop 1 | day high +38% | vwap 30s | tf 1
//   BACK SVRE 1.92 | stop 1.84 | sVWAP 1.7 (+12.9%) | mVWAP 1.41 (+36.2%) | sma 15 1.88 (+2.1%) | ran 18.4% | candle 1 | back 1 | since 6 | green 1 | day high +45% | vwap 30s | tf 1
// `sma N` = the basis and the price against it, `ran` = the furthest a high of the run got above
// the basis so far, `pop N` / `back N` = the day's POPs / BACKs sent on this ticker, `stop` = see
// above, `since N` = candles after the POP candle, `green` = the MACD above its signal at the
// bounce (1 / 0).
// Its twelve inputs and its three plots were the script's last in v48 (v49's two and two follow
// them). Its basis line is hidden until switched on in Style (with TURN's settings it is TURN's
// line).
// v49, the volume test. Operator, 11-26, with two POPs of RAYA (04:27 New York, off a flat base
// with almost no volume: "suitable"; 11:10, at the end of a slow climb on steady volume: "not"):
// "the rvol for that moment should be very high … the stocks which are almost without volume,
// suddenly started popping up. I think we should focus on only such moves".
//   vol      the largest volume among the POP candle and the two candles before it ÷ the average
//            volume of the 20 candles before those three. Three candles, because a pop often
//            takes two or three to reach the mark, and read against the 20 before the POP candle
//            alone its own first candles would water the average down (50 times the base on each
//            of three candles would read 8.5x). A slow climb on steady volume still reads low:
//            RAYA's 11:10 POP reads 6.2x.
//   weak     with the switch on, a POP whose `vol` is under the minimum (10 by default): drawn
//            gray ("pop"), sent with `| weak`, stored and not announced, and it takes no `pop N`.
//            Its BACK is weak too ("bk", `| weak`, no `back N`).
// Both messages carry `| vol 34.5x` after `ran` (a BACK carries its POP's), so the rows can be
// graded by it whatever the switch says. Two cases have no reading: those 20 candles had no
// volume at all (with volume in the three, that POP counts as a surge), or the chart has fewer than 23
// candles (weak). The flag is the script's: `vol` is printed to one decimal, so a 9.96 reads
// `vol 10x` and is weak.
//   POP RAYA 0.58 | sVWAP 0.47 (+23.4%) | sma 15 0.46 (+26.1%) | ran 31.5% | vol 212.4x | candle 1 | pop 1 | day high +29% | vwap 30s | tf 1
//   POP RAYA 0.73 | sVWAP 0.71 (+2.8%) | sma 15 0.68 (+7.4%) | ran 10.5% | vol 6.2x | candle 1 | pop 1 | weak | day high +120% | vwap 30s | tf 1
//   BACK RAYA 0.91 | stop 0.82 | sVWAP 0.88 (+3.4%) | sma 15 0.9 (+1.1%) | ran 150.2% | vol 212.4x | candle 1 | back 1 | since 11 | green 1 | day high +156% | vwap 30s | tf 1
// Measured before building (pop_back_study.py, tables 3–6): among names already on our Momentum
// screen the reading does not sort the POPs (a high +10% above the POP's close follows about as
// many of them in every bucket). That data has no pop out of a stock that was not yet moving,
// which is the case the operator means, so this is their filter to try; the rows will say.
// Its two inputs are the script's last (shown in this group); its two plots are the script's last.
ppOn     = input.bool(true,      "POP setup on (v48): a run pops well above its basis (POP, a heads-up), then comes back to the basis and bounces (BACK, the entry)", group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppTf     = input.timeframe("1",  "POP: the basis's timeframe — its candles are the ones judged; the markers show on that chart, the alerts come from the alert on it", group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppLen    = input.int(15,         "POP: the basis's length (the closes it averages)", minval = 2, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppUp     = input.float(10.0,     "POP: a candle's high at least this % above the basis, in a run of closes above it", minval = 0.5, step = 0.5, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppTol    = input.float(1.0,      "BACK: a low within this % above the basis counts as the pullback reaching it", minval = 0, step = 0.1, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppWaitN  = input.int(20,         "BACK: the bounce comes within N candles after the POP candle (0 = until a close under the basis)", minval = 0, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppMacdOn = input.bool(true,      "BACK: the MACD must be green at the bounce (above its signal line)", group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppFast   = input.int(12,         "BACK: the MACD's fast length", minval = 1, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppSlow   = input.int(26,         "BACK: the MACD's slow length", minval = 2, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppSig    = input.int(9,          "BACK: the MACD's signal length", minval = 1, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppGainOn = input.bool(true,      "POP and BACK: gainers only (the gainer filter at the top)", group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppShow   = input.bool(true,      "POP and BACK: draw the markers (the basis line is hidden until switched on in Style)", group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppVolOn  = input.bool(true,      "POP: only a pop with a volume surge is announced (v49); the others are drawn gray and sent as weak", group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppVolMin = input.float(10.0,     "POP: …the biggest of the POP candle and the two candles before it traded at least this many times the average of the 20 candles before them", minval = 0, step = 0.5, group = "POP and BACK: a pop off the basis and its first pullback (v48)")
ppRun    = ppOn and timeframe.in_seconds(ppTf) == chartSec
// the volume surge at this candle: the largest volume among it and the two candles before it,
// against the average of the 20 candles before those three (no volume at all in those 20 and
// some now counts as a surge)
ppVolTop  = math.max(volume, nz(volume[1]), nz(volume[2]))
ppVolBase = ta.sma(volume, 20)[3]
ppVolX    = ppVolBase > 0 ? ppVolTop / ppVolBase : na
ppSurge   = not na(ppVolBase) and (ppVolBase > 0 ? ppVolTop / ppVolBase >= ppVolMin : ppVolTop > 0)
// v50, the stock's RVol. Operator, 11-28, after the POPs were measured by it (research/ema-vwap/
// pop_entry_study.py, tables 14–15: with a buy stop 5% above the alert the take-profit came first
// for about 20% of POPs on the lowest RVol and 32–34% on the highest, and the POPs that alert on
// a stock with an RVol 1m of about 12,000% or more were the one group positive in both halves):
// "yes, add rvol to the POP alert", then "just add it, not a setting".
// The dashboard's definitions, as the companion rvol.pine computes them:
//   RVol 1m = the volume of the last minute  ÷ (the average day's volume ÷ 390) × 100
//   RVol 5m = the volume of the last 5 minutes ÷ (the average day's volume ÷ 78)  × 100
// where the average day is the regular-hours volume of the chart's own last 20 sessions (the same
// feed on both sides of the division; the first sessions loaded are left out, and under 3 counted
// sessions there is no reading). It is not the dashboard's own number: that one comes from
// Finviz's volume and its 3-month average, and exists only for a name on the Momentum screen; this
// one exists for every watchlist name. Compare the two on the rows before trusting a level.
// A reading only: both messages carry `| rvol1 14250 | rvol5 9800` after `vol` (a BACK carries
// its POP's), nothing is decided by it here. No input, no request; two plots, the script's last,
// shown in the Data Window only. The average covers as many sessions as the chart's history
// holds, up to 20. "The last 5 minutes" is the last five candles: TradingView prints no candle
// for a minute without a trade, so on a thin name or in the pre-market the five reach back
// further, and in a day's first candles into the evening before.
//   POP MNDR 0.84 | sVWAP 0.62 (+35.5%) | sma 15 0.59 (+42.4%) | ran 43.5% | vol 27.6x | rvol1 48210 | rvol5 11975 | candle 1 | pop 1 | day high +44% | vwap 30s | tf 1
//   BACK MNDR 0.97 | stop 0.93 | sVWAP 0.9 (+7.8%) | sma 15 0.96 (+1.0%) | ran 91.2% | vol 27.6x | rvol1 48210 | rvol5 11975 | candle 1 | back 1 | since 9 | green 1 | day high +88% | vwap 30s | tf 1
var ppRvSess = array.new<float>()
var float ppRvRth  = 0.0     // this session's regular-hours volume so far
var int   ppRvDays = 0
if newDay
    if ppRvDays >= 2 and ppRvRth > 0
        array.push(ppRvSess, ppRvRth)
        if array.size(ppRvSess) > 20
            array.shift(ppRvSess)
    ppRvDays += 1
    ppRvRth := 0.0
if session.ismarket
    ppRvRth += volume
float ppRvAdv = array.size(ppRvSess) >= 3 ? array.avg(ppRvSess) : na
ppRvOk1  = timeframe.isintraday and chartSec <= 60 and 60 % chartSec == 0
ppRvOk5  = timeframe.isintraday and chartSec <= 300 and 300 % chartSec == 0
ppRvSum1 = math.sum(volume, ppRvOk1 ? int(60 / chartSec) : 1)
ppRvSum5 = math.sum(volume, ppRvOk5 ? int(300 / chartSec) : 1)
float ppRv1 = ppRvOk1 and ppRvAdv > 0 ? ppRvSum1 / (ppRvAdv / 390) * 100 : na
float ppRv5 = ppRvOk5 and ppRvAdv > 0 ? ppRvSum5 / (ppRvAdv / 78) * 100 : na
ppB      = ta.sma(close, ppLen)
[ppMacdLine, ppSignalLine, ppHist] = ta.macd(close, ppFast, ppSlow, ppSig)
ppGreen  = ppHist > 0
var bool  ppIn      = false   // inside a run: no close under the basis since the close that crossed above it
var float ppRan     = 0.0     // the furthest a high of the run got above the basis, %
var float ppTop     = na      // the run's highest high
var float ppPbLow   = na      // the lowest low after the candle of that high
var bool  ppPopped  = false   // the run has had its POP
var bool  ppWaiting = false   // waiting for the POP's BACK
var int   ppPopBar  = na
var bool  ppTouched = false
var int   ppPopN    = 0       // the day's POPs sent on this ticker (weak ones are not counted)
var int   ppBackN   = 0       // the day's BACKs sent on this ticker (weak ones are not counted)
var float ppPopVol  = na      // the POP's volume reading (ppVolX at the POP candle)
var float ppPopRv1  = na      // the stock's RVol 1m at the POP candle, % (v50)
var float ppPopRv5  = na      // the stock's RVol 5m at the POP candle, % (v50)
var bool  ppWeak    = false   // the run's POP failed the volume test: it and its BACK are weak
if newDay
    ppPopN    := 0
    ppBackN   := 0
    ppIn      := false
    ppWaiting := false
bool  ppPopFire  = false
bool  ppBackFire = false
float ppStop     = na
int   ppAge      = na
if ppRun and not na(ppB) and not na(ppB[1])
    if ppIn and close < ppB
        ppIn      := false
        ppWaiting := false
    else if not ppIn and close > ppB and (close[1] <= ppB[1] or newDay)
        ppIn      := true
        ppRan     := 0.0
        ppTop     := na
        ppPbLow   := na
        ppPopped  := false
        ppWaiting := false
    if ppIn
        ppRan := math.max(ppRan, (high / ppB - 1) * 100)
        // the pullback's low with this candle in it (read before a new high starts it over)
        float ppLowNow = na(ppPbLow) ? low : math.min(ppPbLow, low)
        if not ppPopped
            if ppRan >= ppUp
                // the POP: it uses up the run, whether or not the filters let it send
                ppPopped  := true
                ppWaiting := true
                ppTouched := false
                ppPopBar  := bar_index
                ppPopVol  := ppVolX
                ppPopRv1  := ppRv1
                ppPopRv5  := ppRv5
                ppWeak    := ppVolOn and not ppSurge
                if inWindow and (not ppGainOn or gainer)
                    ppPopFire := true
                    if not ppWeak
                        ppPopN += 1
        else if ppWaiting
            if low <= ppB * (1 + ppTol / 100)
                ppTouched := true
            if ppTouched and close > open and close > ppB and ppB > ppB[1] and (not ppMacdOn or ppGreen)
                // the bounce: it uses up the POP, whether or not the filters let it send
                ppWaiting := false
                if inWindow and (not ppGainOn or gainer)
                    ppBackFire := true
                    ppStop     := ppLowNow - syminfo.mintick
                    ppAge      := bar_index - ppPopBar
                    if not ppWeak
                        ppBackN += 1
            else if ppWaitN > 0 and bar_index - ppPopBar >= ppWaitN
                ppWaiting := false
        if na(ppTop) or high > ppTop
            ppTop   := high
            ppPbLow := na
        else
            ppPbLow := ppLowNow
ppMsg(bool isBack) =>
    string msg = (isBack ? "BACK " : "POP ") + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    if isBack
        msg += " | stop " + str.tostring(ppStop, format.mintick)
    if not na(svwap)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(svwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(svwap) + "%)"
    if not na(mvwap)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(mvwap) + "%)"
    if not na(yvwap)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(yvwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | sma " + str.tostring(ppLen) + " " + str.tostring(ppB, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(ppB) + "%)"
    msg += " | ran " + str.tostring(ppRan, "#.0") + "%"
    if not na(ppPopVol)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(ppPopVol, "#.#") + "x"
    if not na(ppPopRv1)
        msg += " | rvol1 " + str.tostring(math.round(ppPopRv1))
    if not na(ppPopRv5)
        msg += " | rvol5 " + str.tostring(math.round(ppPopRv5))
    msg += " | candle " + ppTf
    if isBack
        msg += " | back " + str.tostring(ppBackN) + " | since " + str.tostring(ppAge) + " | green " + (ppGreen ? "1" : "0")
    else
        msg += " | pop " + str.tostring(ppPopN)
    if ppWeak
        msg += " | weak"
    if not na(dayHighGain)
        msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    msg + " | vwap " + (use30 ? "30s" : "chart") + " | tf " + timeframe.period
if ppPopFire
    alert(ppMsg(false), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if ppBackFire
    alert(ppMsg(true), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plot(ppRun and ppShow ? ppB : na, "POP basis (v48)", color.orange, display = display.none)
plotshape(ppShow and ppPopFire and not ppWeak, "POP (v48)", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.yellow, text = "POP", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(ppShow and ppBackFire and not ppWeak, "BACK (v48)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.aqua, text = "BK", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
// v49 plots go last: the POPs the volume test calls weak, and their BACKs, in gray (sent with `| weak`, stored, not announced).
plotshape(ppShow and ppPopFire and ppWeak, "POP, low volume (v49)", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.gray, text = "pop", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(ppShow and ppBackFire and ppWeak, "BACK after a low-volume POP (v49)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.gray, text = "bk", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
// v50 plots go last: the stock's RVol 1m and 5m in percent, in the Data Window only (they are on another scale than the price, so they are not drawn).
plot(ppOn ? ppRv1 : na, "RVol 1m, % (v50)", color.gray, display = display.data_window)
plot(ppOn ? ppRv5 : na, "RVol 5m, % (v50)", color.gray, display = display.data_window)
